1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:02:03,540
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:08,580
No living being was harmed during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,780
Yenişehir

4
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:16,770
Episode 121

5
00:02:31,885 --> 00:02:34,475
Alps, hey!

6
00:02:35,035 --> 00:02:36,895
Do not oppress the prisoners.

7
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,360
Take these people to the dungeon now.

8
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,760
Bandage their wounds.

9
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:59,100
After beheading Nayman...

10
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:02,780
If there are people whose ransom
will be paid, they will be set free.

11
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:10,630
If there are those among them who want
to repent and enter the religion of Islam...

12
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:17,760
we need their clothes, come on.

13
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,100
Your command, my Bey.

14
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:25,220
Brothers.

15
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:28,260
Are you okay, brothers?

16
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:30,520
Are you okay?

17
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,860
We'll be fine.

18
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,360
We'll be fine.

19
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:41,860
How is he, Kumral Abdal?
Tell me.

20
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:43,780
He will be fine, my Bey.

21
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,680
He will be fine, Inshallah.

22
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:49,110
Yes, we will be fine, Inshallah.

23
00:03:49,110 --> 00:03:50,470
Inshallah.

24
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:52,350
Inshallah.

25
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:53,730
My Bey.

26
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,890
My Bey.

27
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:05,720
Nayman and his army lifted
the siege and withdrew.

28
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,390
It will be the last war.

29
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:11,860
Let him do whatever he wants.

30
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,430
Say what you need to say.

31
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:24,150
Malhun Hatun sent word
from the Kargın tribe.

32
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:25,960
And yet?

33
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,380
Aktemur Bey.

34
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:32,530
He sat on the seat of lordship in
the tribe of Kargın, my Bey.

35
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,010
What?

36
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:48,660
- Boran.
- My Bey.

37
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,360
Summon the Beys...

38
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:52,720
to meet in the court.

39
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,900
Summon Aktemyr from the Kargın tribe.

40
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:02,910
And let the rest come
with me to the palace.

41
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,520
Your command, my Bey.

42
00:05:25,805 --> 00:05:27,915
Hold on, Alps!

43
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:36,200
You struggle.

44
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:38,895
This is my area and you have
no escape from here.

45
00:05:39,245 --> 00:05:41,725
We didn't come to run away,
we came to take your soul, Saveli.

46
00:05:41,775 --> 00:05:43,775
I will cut off your head!

47
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:01,055
Protect your back.

48
00:06:06,265 --> 00:06:07,795
Come on

49
00:06:14,945 --> 00:06:17,055
They are everywhere, my Sultan.

50
00:06:17,505 --> 00:06:21,565
You will kill all the snakes in this palace!

51
00:06:52,065 --> 00:06:54,645
Where is Bala Hatun?

52
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:59,215
We parted ways and she is also looking for
the Sultan Aladdin.

53
00:08:28,795 --> 00:08:32,875
They said, don't say big words.

54
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:35,125
You said you'd cut off my head, right?

55
00:08:35,155 --> 00:08:37,284
Look whose neck the sword touches.

56
00:08:38,315 --> 00:08:40,405
Move while you have the chance.

57
00:08:40,825 --> 00:08:43,164
I will not ask you for
mercy in order to live.

58
00:08:43,335 --> 00:08:44,675
No.

59
00:08:45,335 --> 00:08:47,395
I will not stain my hands with your blood.

60
00:08:47,965 --> 00:08:50,345
Sultan Aladdin will kill you.

61
00:08:51,205 --> 00:08:54,955
Sultan Aladdin will kill you, not me, Saveli.

62
00:08:55,075 --> 00:08:57,295
Your betrayal has been exposed.

63
00:08:59,695 --> 00:09:04,585
Who attacked the palace with his
sword, Bala Hatun? You or me?

64
00:09:07,245 --> 00:09:11,545
This is the evidence of the blood
that was shed in this palace.

65
00:09:15,005 --> 00:09:17,395
What's going on?
What's the matter?

66
00:09:24,175 --> 00:09:27,395
This is the traitor who tried
to kill Sultan Aladdin.

67
00:09:27,875 --> 00:09:29,265
They arrested her.

68
00:09:37,895 --> 00:09:39,215
Come on, move.

69
00:09:39,215 --> 00:09:40,925
It doesn't end here, Saveli.

70
00:09:40,935 --> 00:09:43,445
I will break your bones! Leave me!

71
00:09:46,855 --> 00:09:48,855
You, come here.

72
00:09:51,025 --> 00:09:52,595
Take a unit with you.

73
00:09:53,115 --> 00:09:55,695
And take İsmihan and bring
her to me, come on.

74
00:09:55,975 --> 00:09:57,845
Come on, soldiers.

75
00:10:10,095 --> 00:10:11,985
Nayman made me an offer.

76
00:10:13,605 --> 00:10:16,155
He wants to duel me face to face.

77
00:10:21,015 --> 00:10:22,575
Why, my Bey?

78
00:10:23,315 --> 00:10:25,145
If I defeat him...

79
00:10:26,195 --> 00:10:28,715
his soldiers will leave this land.

80
00:10:29,845 --> 00:10:33,175
But if he defeats me...

81
00:10:34,765 --> 00:10:37,895
Beys and Alps
will pledge allegiance to him.

82
00:10:41,285 --> 00:10:43,935
Can Nayman be trusted, my Bey?

83
00:10:44,655 --> 00:10:46,345
Even if you kill him...

84
00:10:46,355 --> 00:10:50,915
he must have given his soldiers orders
to destroy everything on these lands.

85
00:10:51,715 --> 00:10:53,265
He will keep his promise.

86
00:10:55,395 --> 00:10:58,465
As long as we know he's
going to cheat us...

87
00:10:58,495 --> 00:11:00,535
let us do the same.

88
00:11:00,555 --> 00:11:02,365
Let's attack first.

89
00:11:03,885 --> 00:11:05,985
Even if they will resort to subterfuge...

90
00:11:06,415 --> 00:11:08,215
We must take our precautions.

91
00:11:09,455 --> 00:11:11,765
How we defended Yenişehir...

92
00:11:11,985 --> 00:11:15,425
we will defend all our
properties, as we did in Yenişehir.

93
00:11:18,235 --> 00:11:22,085
Yenişehir resisted because you are here.

94
00:11:22,435 --> 00:11:24,155
But other properties...

95
00:11:24,205 --> 00:11:26,795
You won't be able to stand it.

96
00:11:29,615 --> 00:11:31,115
Let's see.

97
00:11:38,955 --> 00:11:40,485
Karacahisar.

98
00:11:44,165 --> 00:11:45,745
Kulucahisar.

99
00:11:48,905 --> 00:11:50,475
Hisar.

100
00:11:53,815 --> 00:11:55,385
İnegöl.

101
00:11:58,915 --> 00:12:00,415
Bilecik.

102
00:12:03,445 --> 00:12:08,315
Söğüt.

103
00:12:09,685 --> 00:12:12,395
Villages adjacent to
these properties as well...

104
00:12:12,675 --> 00:12:15,035
these will be our defensive campaigns
there.

105
00:12:18,535 --> 00:12:23,555
Look at it well, Alps.

106
00:12:23,735 --> 00:12:26,075
They are the places where
the warriors will settle...

107
00:12:26,095 --> 00:12:28,675
and the places where
the gunpowder will be placed.

108
00:12:28,975 --> 00:12:31,225
They are all drawn on maps.

109
00:12:31,455 --> 00:12:37,135
These show the Beys
who will preside over the property...

110
00:12:40,085 --> 00:12:42,475
but...

111
00:12:44,745 --> 00:12:49,055
This is Marmaracık's defense plan.

112
00:12:50,905 --> 00:12:53,225
It was not for us to give it to Öktem Bey.

113
00:12:56,215 --> 00:13:00,295
We will not leave
Marmaracık to the infidels.

114
00:13:03,145 --> 00:13:07,255
Excuse me, my Bey, but
when did you get this ready?

115
00:13:09,445 --> 00:13:15,035
We rest only for a short time
so that the whole Islamic world can rest.

116
00:13:20,855 --> 00:13:24,415
We will fight a war where there is no rest anymore.

117
00:13:24,955 --> 00:13:26,735
Be prepared.

118
00:13:36,905 --> 00:13:38,985
This is our defensive campaign.

119
00:13:39,815 --> 00:13:42,995
Now it is the turn of our
offensive campaign.

120
00:13:57,075 --> 00:13:58,585
Karancu.

121
00:13:59,385 --> 00:14:04,415
You will send three messengers
to the regions of the Beys.

122
00:14:04,455 --> 00:14:08,875
I want all soldiers
over there to come here....

123
00:14:09,745 --> 00:14:13,315
secretly.

124
00:14:13,825 --> 00:14:15,805
When Osman dies...

125
00:14:16,045 --> 00:14:19,295
they will spread my wrath on this land.

126
00:14:20,995 --> 00:14:22,575
Shaman.

127
00:14:22,975 --> 00:14:25,345
As soon as possible...

128
00:14:25,655 --> 00:14:31,155
Prepare a poison that will prevent
Osman's eyes from seeing.

129
00:14:37,675 --> 00:14:42,715
Nayman, who defeated the Beys,
will withdraw his soldiers from their lands to ours.

130
00:14:43,535 --> 00:14:45,955
He will set up camp for them here.

131
00:14:46,615 --> 00:14:49,525
Let's be there for him.

132
00:14:50,025 --> 00:14:51,615
And let's pounce on them.

133
00:14:51,615 --> 00:14:54,005
No, we will not attack them.

134
00:14:54,525 --> 00:14:56,985
Right now, it looks like Nayman
will keep his promise.

135
00:14:57,055 --> 00:14:59,555
For this reason, he would not reveal
the location of his camp.

136
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:07,225
But to find out where the units that
will attack us are stationed...

137
00:15:07,985 --> 00:15:12,305
Warriors will be sent to those areas.

138
00:15:15,275 --> 00:15:17,345
When units start attacking...

139
00:15:17,385 --> 00:15:19,455
Warriors (Alps) will attack those camps.

140
00:15:19,955 --> 00:15:23,475
Come on, let everyone go to work.

141
00:15:30,965 --> 00:15:32,555
Duran.

142
00:15:34,915 --> 00:15:36,285
My Bey.

143
00:15:48,045 --> 00:15:50,135
I have to fight Nayman.

144
00:15:52,195 --> 00:15:53,515
Look.

145
00:15:54,545 --> 00:15:56,255
Is he thinking of a trick?
Find out.

146
00:15:56,365 --> 00:15:58,065
Your command, my Bey

147
00:16:07,705 --> 00:16:10,275
Öktem tribe

148
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:16,750
Won't you bless Aktemur, Hatuns?

149
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,310
Ayşe Hatun.

150
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:22,710
Why is your face so frowning?
What is so sad about this?

151
00:16:22,930 --> 00:16:24,700
He is my son.

152
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,950
I deal with him as I like.

153
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:33,940
Aktemur.

154
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:36,360
Do you know what you did?

155
00:16:40,850 --> 00:16:43,880
These things are always
your idea, Bengi Hatun.

156
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,940
You should have consulted
Osman Bey before, Aktemur.

157
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,400
It is enough!

158
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,540
My mother.

159
00:16:57,970 --> 00:16:59,480
My uncle's wife.

160
00:17:00,690 --> 00:17:02,480
I am not a child.

161
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:04,290
I know what I'm doing.

162
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,300
And you both know that I have
become the Bey of the Kargın tribe.

163
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,970
Aktemur.

164
00:17:16,579 --> 00:17:18,079
We know, we know.

165
00:17:19,089 --> 00:17:20,960
But, know this...

166
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,368
The news must have reached Osman Bey
by now.

167
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:28,210
Let's see if you can speak
comfortably in front of him like this.

168
00:17:33,810 --> 00:17:36,980
It is true that I sat on the chair
without telling my uncle.

169
00:17:39,110 --> 00:17:41,160
But there is nothing wrong with this.

170
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:44,020
Aktemur.

171
00:17:44,050 --> 00:17:46,550
The wrong thing is not you
sitting on the chair.

172
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:48,940
Rather, it is you moving
according to your whims.

173
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:58,080
If there's a campaign or something
you know of, let us know.

174
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,360
Otherwise, the end of this matter is bad.

175
00:18:09,010 --> 00:18:12,100
Has the sovereign's seat
ever been left empty, Malhun Hatun?

176
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:17,990
I am responsible for the result
of the work I have done.

177
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,580
And I have an answer for every question.

178
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,920
May I come in, my Bey?

179
00:18:27,190 --> 00:18:28,570
Come in.

180
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,600
My Bey.

181
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,870
Osman Bey has sent news.

182
00:18:37,590 --> 00:18:39,420
He is waiting for you in the Divan.

183
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,070
Ready my horse, let's get out quickly.

184
00:18:53,130 --> 00:18:54,720
Your command, my Bey.

185
00:19:15,885 --> 00:19:17,705
- Sultan...
- Shut up!

186
00:19:25,985 --> 00:19:30,785
You will tell me all the things
that happen in my palace.

187
00:19:32,165 --> 00:19:35,755
Whether your heads stay in place depends
on what you're going to say.

188
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:38,415
If you say the words incompletely...

189
00:19:39,155 --> 00:19:42,205
I will hang your head at
the entrance to Konya.

190
00:19:45,585 --> 00:19:47,255
You tell me first, Vizier.

191
00:19:47,335 --> 00:19:51,185
My Sultan, Osman Bey is
after rebellion again.

192
00:19:52,645 --> 00:19:55,945
And now he has sent his wife to kill you.

193
00:19:56,135 --> 00:19:57,945
He is lying, my Sultan.

194
00:19:58,545 --> 00:20:01,045
Actually, the one who wants to
kill you is Saveli.

195
00:20:03,145 --> 00:20:04,945
His loyalty is not to you.

196
00:20:06,545 --> 00:20:08,115
It's for Nayman.

197
00:20:08,215 --> 00:20:10,105
Osman Bey has warned you.

198
00:20:10,145 --> 00:20:14,195
I'm tired of these games.

199
00:20:17,505 --> 00:20:20,015
I will not give you my soul...

200
00:20:21,655 --> 00:20:23,225
nor my throne.

201
00:20:25,925 --> 00:20:29,505
You cannot see the traitor
standing before your eyes.

202
00:20:33,305 --> 00:20:34,665
Mother Sultan.

203
00:20:36,665 --> 00:20:38,435
She's in the palace now.

204
00:20:40,765 --> 00:20:42,065
Where?

205
00:20:46,165 --> 00:20:51,555
Is there no end to the lies you tell
to survive, Bala Hatun?

206
00:20:54,615 --> 00:20:58,865
My Sultan, let me
cut off her head now!

207
00:21:18,665 --> 00:21:22,705
Traitor, you will be
drenched in your own blood.

208
00:21:31,655 --> 00:21:37,175
If something happens, we'll kill Sultan Aladdin
and Bala at the same moment, get ready.

209
00:21:40,195 --> 00:21:41,525
Now!

210
00:21:41,655 --> 00:21:44,195
You will not be able to escape my wrath!

211
00:22:10,165 --> 00:22:12,735
I thought you would
never come, Mother Sultan.

212
00:22:14,055 --> 00:22:17,055
The snake's head is here, but the tail is
everywhere, Bala Hatun!

213
00:22:43,545 --> 00:22:45,895
You will not escape my wrath, Sultan.

214
00:22:45,955 --> 00:22:48,085
I'm sending your head to Nayman.

215
00:23:08,195 --> 00:23:12,255
If it weren't for this brave warrior of Osman,
we wouldn't have been able to get here.

216
00:23:35,895 --> 00:23:40,195
The price of betrayal is your soul.

217
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:52,465
If I could kill you and take Konya,
all the people would be forgiven.

218
00:23:54,055 --> 00:23:59,335
Now, in order to take Konya,
all the people must be killed.

219
00:23:59,865 --> 00:24:05,395
Whoever seeks my soul
will first lose his soul.

220
00:24:06,505 --> 00:24:11,895
And whoever thinks of killing the people
will not even have a grave.

221
00:24:33,235 --> 00:24:35,125
Are you okay, my Sultan?

222
00:24:36,055 --> 00:24:37,945
I'm fine, mother.

223
00:24:38,225 --> 00:24:39,545
Fine.

224
00:24:40,855 --> 00:24:43,385
We can't trust anyone.

225
00:24:43,785 --> 00:24:47,365
They nested everywhere in the palace.

226
00:24:49,365 --> 00:24:51,915
I will crush all of their heads.

227
00:24:53,465 --> 00:24:58,885
Bring everyone in front of me whoever was
sending regards to Saveli...

228
00:25:01,235 --> 00:25:04,595
and all those who stand behind him.

229
00:25:04,895 --> 00:25:06,865
Everyone has value in his own eyes.

230
00:25:06,935 --> 00:25:08,485
I want them all.

231
00:25:08,595 --> 00:25:10,985
Your command, my Sultan.

232
00:25:15,975 --> 00:25:19,845
I will behead them all.

233
00:25:38,750 --> 00:25:41,500
Osman Bey is coming!

234
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:47,700
Salam Alaikum.

235
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:51,340
Alaikum Salam.

236
00:25:58,980 --> 00:26:00,570
Please be seated.

237
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:12,500
The court opened with the ninety-nine
names of Allah Almighty...

238
00:26:12,970 --> 00:26:17,540
who made us responsible for
war, not for victory.

239
00:26:18,510 --> 00:26:21,270
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

240
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,860
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

241
00:26:25,450 --> 00:26:28,730
Tell me now, what is the condition of our country?

242
00:26:30,420 --> 00:26:31,980
You tell me, Uraz Bey.

243
00:26:32,030 --> 00:26:33,380
My Bey.

244
00:26:34,170 --> 00:26:36,380
People aren't fine at all.

245
00:26:37,050 --> 00:26:40,250
Nayman's presence has
harmed the business.

246
00:26:41,290 --> 00:26:42,880
Bayram Bey.

247
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,550
You tell me.

248
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:46,890
The situation is the same
in Kulucahisar, my Bey.

249
00:26:46,930 --> 00:26:48,270
One complaint.

250
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,550
Convoys no longer pass through
and trade has stopped.

251
00:26:53,660 --> 00:26:56,750
Well, what about the tribes?
What are the conditions of the tribes?

252
00:26:57,770 --> 00:26:59,150
My Bey.

253
00:26:59,270 --> 00:27:03,600
The people of the tribe take the goods to the city
and bring them back without selling them.

254
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:07,010
Merchants do not have the
power to buy and sell.

255
00:27:07,050 --> 00:27:10,080
They all say the same
thing to the tribesmen.

256
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:13,990
"Our profit is not enough to buy"

257
00:27:16,650 --> 00:27:18,990
Don't you have anything to say?

258
00:27:21,230 --> 00:27:27,800
The chief of the army who was not at the head
of his army when they defended Yenişehir.

259
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,220
Don't you have anything to say?

260
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:41,310
You don't even know the condition
of the people you rule.

261
00:27:42,930 --> 00:27:44,480
What is your advantage?

262
00:27:44,770 --> 00:27:46,860
Is it leaving me alone?

263
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:59,900
Did you ask my permission to
remove you from your job?

264
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:06,000
Did I make you sit in that chair?

265
00:28:06,290 --> 00:28:08,590
My Bey, I sat on it so the
chair wouldn't be empty.

266
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,650
You were my nephew at your first mistake.

267
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,400
I forgave you with one slap.

268
00:28:15,950 --> 00:28:17,210
However...

269
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:23,050
You have no place in my
family or in the court.

270
00:28:23,740 --> 00:28:25,250
Get out now.

271
00:28:26,390 --> 00:28:27,100
My Bey.

272
00:28:27,150 --> 00:28:28,490
Get out!

273
00:29:12,190 --> 00:29:14,460
The situation of the people is difficult.

274
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:18,570
Tell me.

275
00:29:18,940 --> 00:29:21,220
What measures have you
taken in this regard?

276
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:26,660
We met with the elders of the Achaeans, and took
aid to the merchants from the treasury.

277
00:29:27,530 --> 00:29:29,800
You're just killing flies.

278
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:33,900
The main issue is draining the swamp.

279
00:29:35,900 --> 00:29:39,580
We're ready to do as you command, my Bey.
These problems will surely be solved

280
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:43,840
But you never talk about the matter
of Nayman.

281
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:45,980
- Boran.
- My Bey.

282
00:29:46,030 --> 00:29:47,840
Hand out the maps relating to Nayman.

283
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:49,430
Your command, my Bey.

284
00:29:56,300 --> 00:29:59,850
Beys, look at the maps carefully.

285
00:30:02,540 --> 00:30:04,700
Defense plans are all in these maps.

286
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,580
Consult well with the Beys.

287
00:30:08,150 --> 00:30:11,850
And tomorrow you will be in the
field of war with your armies.

288
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:18,790
However...

289
00:30:20,050 --> 00:30:30,100
It's clear that the main distress is
with the people.

290
00:30:32,170 --> 00:30:34,030
We will now be on their side.

291
00:30:35,420 --> 00:30:42,510
I would even go to them
myself and see their problems.

292
00:30:44,150 --> 00:30:47,720
And you too will come with me in disguise.

293
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:51,580
You will spread among the people
and get to know all their problems one by one.

294
00:30:54,900 --> 00:31:00,460
The distress of the people is more
important than the affliction of Nayman.

295
00:31:03,460 --> 00:31:04,990
Court is over.

296
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:12,040
Summon Malhun Hatun.

297
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,180
Your command, my Bey.

298
00:31:23,140 --> 00:31:25,160
Marmaracık Castle

299
00:32:09,975 --> 00:32:11,175
Tell me.

300
00:32:11,185 --> 00:32:14,275
Your army is out on the
road, Commander Nayman.

301
00:32:15,155 --> 00:32:17,715
I'm not asking about
the situation out there.

302
00:32:18,285 --> 00:32:20,295
They will come from everywhere.

303
00:32:20,815 --> 00:32:23,675
Tell me about the situation inside.

304
00:32:24,785 --> 00:32:27,845
Aktemur, nephew of Osman.

305
00:32:28,235 --> 00:32:32,715
He sat on Öktam's chair without
Osman's knowledge.

306
00:32:36,415 --> 00:32:40,965
Aktemur wants to fly on his wings, then.

307
00:32:42,755 --> 00:32:44,645
And what does his uncle say about this?

308
00:32:44,735 --> 00:32:47,585
Osman held a court.

309
00:32:49,455 --> 00:32:54,305
Aktemur was also summoned to the court.

310
00:32:57,395 --> 00:33:00,915
He clearly acknowledges
Aktemur's sovereignty.

311
00:33:02,505 --> 00:33:06,785
Osman will never accept the sovereignty of Aktemur.

312
00:33:08,175 --> 00:33:10,005
His pride prevents this.

313
00:33:16,615 --> 00:33:19,875
Commander Nayman, there is news
from our spies in Yenişehir, sir.

314
00:33:19,965 --> 00:33:21,765
They heard it while people were
talking about it in the bazaar.

315
00:33:21,785 --> 00:33:24,375
Osman expelled Aktemur from the Court.

316
00:33:38,895 --> 00:33:44,955
Osman
walks alone into my fist.

317
00:33:52,855 --> 00:33:54,675
If you'll excuse me...

318
00:33:55,745 --> 00:33:59,635
I want to talk to you alone about
a topic, Sultan.

319
00:34:27,734 --> 00:34:29,045
Say it.

320
00:34:29,873 --> 00:34:35,925
Nayman's intention is to take over our
vast lands, my Sultan.

321
00:34:40,355 --> 00:34:42,245
For this reason, he wanted to kill you.

322
00:34:44,655 --> 00:34:47,855
Nayman won't stop until he's done.

323
00:34:49,145 --> 00:34:50,904
In this situation...

324
00:34:51,804 --> 00:34:56,355
I have neither the strength nor
the ability to face Nayman, Bala Hatun.

325
00:34:59,475 --> 00:35:01,355
It is not important, my Sultan.

326
00:35:02,595 --> 00:35:04,485
What you have is enough for us.

327
00:35:05,615 --> 00:35:09,515
The believers defeated the unbelieving
many times.

328
00:35:12,855 --> 00:35:16,155
Living under Nayman's
banner is not a solution.

329
00:35:17,285 --> 00:35:21,395
Rebellion against the
oppressor is part of faith.

330
00:35:28,815 --> 00:35:31,445
There is news from the
borderlands, Mother Sultan.

331
00:35:31,495 --> 00:35:34,095
Osman and Nayman will fight.

332
00:35:39,925 --> 00:35:41,165
Alright.

333
00:35:44,395 --> 00:35:48,045
We'll go to the borderlands without
wasting any time, Celali.

334
00:35:48,915 --> 00:35:50,735
Do your preparations.

335
00:35:52,735 --> 00:35:54,235
They will fight.

336
00:35:56,335 --> 00:35:58,175
And we'll share what's left.

337
00:36:15,135 --> 00:36:17,645
You start the war first...

338
00:36:17,745 --> 00:36:20,225
and you gather allies
after that, Bala Hatun.

339
00:36:27,335 --> 00:36:30,885
I will give Osman Bey
five thousand soldiers...

340
00:36:31,295 --> 00:36:35,635
and twenty wagons of arms
in case of war.

341
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:42,435
Thank you, Sultan.

342
00:36:43,795 --> 00:36:46,395
The army you provide will
be a means for good.

343
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:52,765
Now...

344
00:36:54,505 --> 00:36:56,525
I have another request from you.

345
00:36:59,405 --> 00:37:01,435
What more do you ask for, Bala Hatun?

346
00:37:02,565 --> 00:37:05,125
I need you to write a letter
to Ghazan Khan.

347
00:37:27,465 --> 00:37:29,535
What letter is this?

348
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:32,185
What is your intention?

349
00:37:36,815 --> 00:37:38,205
My intention is executing...

350
00:37:39,845 --> 00:37:45,065
the campaign that will end the war before
it begins, by order of Osman Bey.

351
00:37:59,135 --> 00:38:01,055
Kurudere Location

352
00:38:07,665 --> 00:38:11,415
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

353
00:38:12,115 --> 00:38:14,995
Come on, I have fabrics.

354
00:38:15,675 --> 00:38:17,035
This is good

355
00:38:17,065 --> 00:38:18,585
Cut this.

356
00:38:26,785 --> 00:38:28,515
How is the business?

357
00:38:28,625 --> 00:38:31,165
Thank Allah very
much, my Bey, we are managing.

358
00:38:32,525 --> 00:38:35,075
There's nothing left on
your table but hemp cloths.

359
00:38:35,185 --> 00:38:36,775
Don't you have velvet fabrics?

360
00:38:36,915 --> 00:38:38,755
Where do I get it, my sister?

361
00:38:38,785 --> 00:38:41,505
Merchants come and offer us velvet fabrics.

362
00:38:41,935 --> 00:38:45,035
They then lead their caravans
to Bursa and Iznik.

363
00:38:45,135 --> 00:38:47,935
We do not have the
possibility to buy velvet fabrics.

364
00:38:52,305 --> 00:38:54,115
What breaks your strength?

365
00:38:54,295 --> 00:38:56,805
War first, then shop rent.

366
00:38:58,425 --> 00:39:01,005
I earn forty coins or hardly earn them

367
00:39:01,035 --> 00:39:04,075
I pay twenty of them as rent for the shop.

368
00:39:11,925 --> 00:39:14,485
- May Allah help you.
- Thank you.

369
00:39:14,535 --> 00:39:16,775
Cut a little bit of this cloth.

370
00:39:18,315 --> 00:39:23,395
They will look at us and go as long
as we don't have the goods, brother.

371
00:39:25,125 --> 00:39:26,965
We hardly pay the rent for the shops.

372
00:39:27,165 --> 00:39:28,795
We can't manage things with what we have.

373
00:39:28,845 --> 00:39:31,845
We will close the shops before
the end of this month, brother.

374
00:39:46,225 --> 00:39:48,105
- Here you go, sister.
- Thank you.

375
00:39:48,305 --> 00:39:50,155
Thank you.

376
00:39:52,285 --> 00:39:56,495
Yes, tell me what puts you in
such a difficult situation?

377
00:39:57,165 --> 00:39:59,755
What puts you in such distress?

378
00:40:02,205 --> 00:40:04,285
Not what, but who, my Bey.

379
00:40:07,845 --> 00:40:09,045
Who is he?

380
00:40:09,075 --> 00:40:10,825
It's Osman Bey.

381
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:18,035
Osman Bey, then.

382
00:40:18,075 --> 00:40:19,725
And what did Osman Bey do?

383
00:40:19,825 --> 00:40:21,095
What can Osman Bey do?

384
00:40:21,145 --> 00:40:22,965
The infidels pounced on our heads.

385
00:40:22,975 --> 00:40:28,505
Trade stopped and revenues decreased,
but expenses did not decrease, my sister.

386
00:40:30,175 --> 00:40:32,065
Rents have weighed heavily
on our shoulders.

387
00:40:32,245 --> 00:40:35,255
Who is the commander of this district?
It's Osman Bey.

388
00:40:36,845 --> 00:40:38,385
Can't he protect the merchants?

389
00:40:41,435 --> 00:40:43,025
Halil.

390
00:40:43,035 --> 00:40:46,145
Osman Bey will fight the head
of the infidels Nayman soon.

391
00:40:46,435 --> 00:40:48,935
Will he still have time for
us while he sharpens swords?

392
00:40:49,135 --> 00:40:50,805
You're right, blacksmith.

393
00:40:51,845 --> 00:40:54,455
No, Halil says the right thing.

394
00:40:56,715 --> 00:40:58,555
If you let all these enemies
come after you...

395
00:40:58,625 --> 00:41:02,345
and take care of external
problems for the sake of a dream..

396
00:41:02,595 --> 00:41:05,795
You should take care of
internal problems as well.

397
00:41:07,335 --> 00:41:09,835
Look, the Bey understood me and you didn't.

398
00:41:15,825 --> 00:41:19,425
Say, is this the case for all merchants?

399
00:41:19,835 --> 00:41:23,595
This is the condition of all merchants who
do not have their shops, my Bey.

400
00:41:26,355 --> 00:41:27,685
Okay.

401
00:41:43,315 --> 00:41:45,825
Bring death!

402
00:41:48,085 --> 00:41:50,625
Bring death!

403
00:41:51,845 --> 00:41:54,415
Bring death!

404
00:42:11,435 --> 00:42:12,955
Shaman.

405
00:42:14,450 --> 00:42:16,470
Is the poison ready yet?

406
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:18,660
It'll be ready
tomorrow, Commander Nayman.

407
00:42:21,110 --> 00:42:22,690
Tonight...

408
00:42:23,250 --> 00:42:25,800
Patience increases the effect
of the poison.

409
00:42:27,210 --> 00:42:31,110
This poison will bring
disability and death to Osman.

410
00:42:34,370 --> 00:42:36,770
And the verdict is mine.

411
00:42:38,240 --> 00:42:41,540
I will kill Osman with this poison.

412
00:42:41,810 --> 00:42:44,910
But it will end tonight.

413
00:42:45,640 --> 00:42:49,890
My army shall gather tomorrow,
and the seal shall be in my hands.

414
00:42:50,310 --> 00:42:53,540
All Mongols will unite behind me.

415
00:42:54,380 --> 00:43:00,370
Then I will not only wipe out Osman alone
from these lands, but all the Turks.

416
00:43:02,770 --> 00:43:09,170
Konya, the border regions
and the whole world will belong to me!

417
00:43:09,600 --> 00:43:13,620
All your soldiers are
eagerly awaiting this, sir.

418
00:43:14,040 --> 00:43:15,940
Sacrifice horses.

419
00:43:16,650 --> 00:43:21,400
All soldiers will drink
horse blood tonight.

420
00:43:22,330 --> 00:43:25,340
They will dedicate it to
the god of heaven.

421
00:43:26,350 --> 00:43:29,860
When victory is mine tomorrow...

422
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:37,590
I will drink the blood that will flow from
Osman's head and offer it to the God of Heaven.

423
00:43:54,810 --> 00:43:56,390
Come on, pay the tribute.

424
00:43:56,750 --> 00:43:58,060
What tribute?

425
00:43:58,110 --> 00:43:59,900
I can't even pay my shop rent.

426
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:01,170
What do we have to do
with your rent?

427
00:44:01,190 --> 00:44:04,540
Either you pay tribute or
you give up your life.

428
00:44:08,020 --> 00:44:09,320
Don't do it, Aghas.

429
00:44:18,210 --> 00:44:20,230
Prepare the double next time.

430
00:44:21,220 --> 00:44:24,350
Otherwise, we wouldn't be
content with taking your soul.

431
00:44:31,810 --> 00:44:33,390
Ali Agha.

432
00:44:33,460 --> 00:44:34,940
Is your tribute (tax) ready?

433
00:44:34,970 --> 00:44:36,210
Don't do it, what tribute?

434
00:44:39,210 --> 00:44:42,020
Aren't you afraid for your son, Ali?

435
00:44:43,650 --> 00:44:45,210
Father, don't.

436
00:44:49,380 --> 00:44:52,500
Good.

437
00:45:00,120 --> 00:45:02,210
I break that hand that extends to
what does not belong to you.

438
00:45:02,250 --> 00:45:04,120
Are you the one who will break it?

439
00:45:04,240 --> 00:45:06,130
Yes, I will break it.

440
00:45:17,110 --> 00:45:18,690
Come here, walk.

441
00:45:30,010 --> 00:45:32,110
If I see you here again....

442
00:45:39,090 --> 00:45:40,310
It didn't end here.

443
00:45:40,360 --> 00:45:42,030
He's still talking!

444
00:45:42,110 --> 00:45:43,810
Walk!

445
00:45:46,460 --> 00:45:48,060
He's still talking.

446
00:45:48,210 --> 00:45:49,740
Are you okay?

447
00:46:01,460 --> 00:46:02,970
May Allah be pleased with you, my Bey.

448
00:46:02,990 --> 00:46:04,990
May Allah be pleased with you too.

449
00:46:05,010 --> 00:46:07,960
Who are you? Where did you come from
and where are you going?

450
00:46:09,710 --> 00:46:11,980
We come from Allah and return to Him.

451
00:46:12,080 --> 00:46:13,250
We are traveling.

452
00:46:13,260 --> 00:46:16,760
Yes, we all come from Him
and return to Him.

453
00:46:16,840 --> 00:46:19,340
But not all of us have these advantages.

454
00:46:19,540 --> 00:46:21,690
Say it, and who are you?

455
00:46:22,660 --> 00:46:25,740
We came here to ask for work, but...

456
00:46:25,990 --> 00:46:29,660
when we saw your condition
like this, we couldn't say it.

457
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:33,900
Anyway, may Allah make it easy for
all of you, we have a long way to go.

458
00:46:33,910 --> 00:46:35,910
Come on, Hatun.

459
00:46:36,660 --> 00:46:39,690
It's true what you say, we
have no work to do for you.

460
00:46:41,060 --> 00:46:44,140
But we also don't allow travelers
to leave hungry like that.

461
00:46:44,360 --> 00:46:48,510
Especially in the time of
blessed Ramadan and after what you did.

462
00:46:53,940 --> 00:46:58,070
Hatun, he's inviting us to iftaar.

463
00:46:58,160 --> 00:46:59,400
So, let's go, my Bey.

464
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:01,440
Good.

465
00:47:01,890 --> 00:47:04,140
Halil, run home and tell your mother.

466
00:47:04,190 --> 00:47:07,760
Tell her we have two guests, come on, son.

467
00:47:10,440 --> 00:47:12,900
Come on traveler, there's a
little left for iftaar.

468
00:47:12,960 --> 00:47:14,960
Help me to pack up the shop.

469
00:47:15,210 --> 00:47:16,510
Come on, then.

470
00:47:16,560 --> 00:47:21,890
I will not allow anyone to say that
Ali Agha left his guests hungry.

471
00:47:28,610 --> 00:47:31,190
- Come on, then.
- Take this.

472
00:47:35,440 --> 00:47:37,490
Damascus

473
00:48:14,750 --> 00:48:17,330
This is where the deal was
made with Bayındır.

474
00:48:21,180 --> 00:48:22,480
We'll wait.

475
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:31,780
Talay must be waiting for me.

476
00:48:33,980 --> 00:48:35,780
Are you the merchant?

477
00:48:36,150 --> 00:48:37,700
Yes. It's me.

478
00:48:42,700 --> 00:48:44,400
Follow us, merchant.

479
00:48:46,650 --> 00:48:48,400
Only you

480
00:48:52,550 --> 00:48:57,130
Soldier, watch your treatment of
Nayman's obedient servant.

481
00:48:57,770 --> 00:49:01,000
The price of your insolence will be
your beheading, to say the least.

482
00:49:01,040 --> 00:49:05,020
Either I come with my men, or I don't.
Go tell Talay.

483
00:49:05,130 --> 00:49:07,130
Talay, the merchant just said.

484
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:10,030
My men are no different from me.

485
00:49:11,130 --> 00:49:13,680
If the merchant
comes, they will come with him.

486
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:17,200
Otherwise, he will not come.

487
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:22,280
How do I know you're
not playing a game?

488
00:49:24,150 --> 00:49:27,730
I tell you I come up with the name Nayman,
and you still say it's a game.

489
00:49:28,820 --> 00:49:30,590
Look at this.

490
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:34,150
How many of these are there in the world?

491
00:49:34,200 --> 00:49:36,090
He gave it to me.

492
00:49:36,130 --> 00:49:38,680
You're making me wait for no reason, soldier.
That's an insult.

493
00:49:38,710 --> 00:49:42,880
And the insult directed at me is
directed at Nayman, too, so you know that.

494
00:49:45,150 --> 00:49:46,680
What are you going to do?

495
00:50:08,075 --> 00:50:10,825
Oh my.

496
00:50:17,875 --> 00:50:19,195
Hüseyin.

497
00:50:19,945 --> 00:50:24,395
When we save ourselves, Inshallah...

498
00:50:24,395 --> 00:50:28,395
remind me to kill you before Nayman.

499
00:50:29,685 --> 00:50:32,255
Sir, I don't understand
what you are saying.

500
00:50:32,535 --> 00:50:34,535
And what do you understand, Hüseyin?

501
00:50:34,795 --> 00:50:36,825
What do you understand?

502
00:50:36,895 --> 00:50:40,975
But I'll explain and I'll
cut off your head.

503
00:50:44,795 --> 00:50:46,145
My Bey.

504
00:50:47,225 --> 00:50:49,445
My head is for you.

505
00:50:49,545 --> 00:50:55,625
But if you're talking about catching us,
they slipped like snakes.

506
00:50:56,975 --> 00:50:59,105
I never noticed they were after us.

507
00:50:59,405 --> 00:51:00,735
No!

508
00:51:03,945 --> 00:51:05,945
But you had to watch out, Hüseyin.

509
00:51:06,625 --> 00:51:09,285
Look, we didn't have the ingot anymore,
and we couldn't solve the Damascus thing.

510
00:51:09,325 --> 00:51:11,345
We only have our heads above our bodies.

511
00:51:12,025 --> 00:51:14,165
And that's because of
Osman's justice.

512
00:51:29,145 --> 00:51:30,925
However, Hüseyin...

513
00:51:31,145 --> 00:51:36,175
I think it's time to run away.

514
00:51:39,775 --> 00:51:41,775
Warrior brother, come a little.

515
00:51:50,075 --> 00:51:54,395
You arrested us and tied us here
since the morning while we were fasting.

516
00:51:54,475 --> 00:51:58,005
Untie us a little, so that the
blood flows through our bodies.

517
00:51:58,025 --> 00:52:00,025
Sit quietly and don't make me kill you.

518
00:52:02,945 --> 00:52:07,445
Well, we made a
mistake, but we are not infidels.

519
00:52:07,575 --> 00:52:10,075
Have pity on us, brother warrior.

520
00:52:10,075 --> 00:52:13,395
Thank Turgut Bey that he
left you to be judged by Osman Bey.

521
00:52:13,495 --> 00:52:14,555
You want to rest.

522
00:52:14,595 --> 00:52:16,125
You will rest when you die.

523
00:52:16,145 --> 00:52:18,405
I ask for Allah's forgiveness
and repent to Him.

524
00:52:18,445 --> 00:52:21,445
You are a Muslim and I am a Muslim.

525
00:52:22,525 --> 00:52:24,225
Pity us a little.

526
00:52:25,045 --> 00:52:27,795
At least change the location of the rope.

527
00:52:40,795 --> 00:52:42,125
You traitor.

528
00:52:42,195 --> 00:52:44,025
The other is coming, my Bey!

529
00:52:56,275 --> 00:52:58,245
I repent to Him.

530
00:52:58,325 --> 00:53:00,325
And we are fasting!

531
00:53:03,475 --> 00:53:05,475
Hüseyin Bey.

532
00:53:07,140 --> 00:53:14,840
This means that if we depended
on you, we would not survive.

533
00:53:17,540 --> 00:53:21,190
Let's go, he's passed out,
let's go before he gets him back.

534
00:53:22,040 --> 00:53:24,360
We have to make them lose
track of us as soon as possible.

535
00:53:25,190 --> 00:53:26,990
- Come on, my Bey.
- Come on.

536
00:53:28,540 --> 00:53:30,570
Did Osman Bey
get very angry?

537
00:53:32,480 --> 00:53:34,530
He didn't stop at anger, Alçiçek.

538
00:53:34,930 --> 00:53:36,780
He kicked me out of the court.

539
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:40,610
He kicked me out of the court in
front of all those Alps and Beys.

540
00:53:43,190 --> 00:53:45,460
What do you say, Aktemur?

541
00:53:47,510 --> 00:53:49,040
Yes, mother.

542
00:53:50,090 --> 00:53:52,480
My uncle accuses me
of neglecting my mission.

543
00:53:52,520 --> 00:53:54,520
I was not even allowed to speak.

544
00:54:03,410 --> 00:54:04,910
Don't bow your head.

545
00:54:05,590 --> 00:54:09,320
If your uncle isn't
behind you, I'm here, son.

546
00:54:09,500 --> 00:54:11,500
And the Kargın tribe, too.

547
00:54:12,490 --> 00:54:13,990
I know, mother, I know.

548
00:54:14,590 --> 00:54:16,260
I will not disappoint you.

549
00:54:20,510 --> 00:54:22,660
This is not the time to stop.

550
00:54:23,460 --> 00:54:27,410
I had made a promise to Kargın Beys
before you sat in the chair of Beyhood.

551
00:54:27,740 --> 00:54:29,090
Promise what, mother?

552
00:54:30,030 --> 00:54:32,260
Since the seat of sovereignty
has found its owner...

553
00:54:32,305 --> 00:54:35,635
the time has come for revenge for
dear Öktam and the warriors.

554
00:54:35,680 --> 00:54:37,000
Mother.

555
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:44,070
I say we'll take Marmaracık from the hand
of that dishonorable Nayman, Alçiçek.

556
00:54:44,710 --> 00:54:49,290
That coward killed our Bey and our
warriors and took our property.

557
00:54:50,190 --> 00:54:53,560
We will not sit still like this.

558
00:54:54,150 --> 00:54:55,100
Right?

559
00:54:56,640 --> 00:54:57,940
No.

560
00:54:58,500 --> 00:55:00,030
Our wound is recent.

561
00:55:00,990 --> 00:55:03,040
And Aktemur just became a Bey.

562
00:55:03,210 --> 00:55:05,390
Is there an old and new rule?

563
00:55:06,210 --> 00:55:08,240
It is not right for us to stop now.

564
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:12,750
Do you want us to break our
promise from day one?

565
00:55:14,610 --> 00:55:18,440
Aktemur, do you think like Alçiçek?

566
00:55:27,800 --> 00:55:29,960
As long as there is a promise made...

567
00:55:32,260 --> 00:55:33,760
We'll take Marmaracık.

568
00:55:35,200 --> 00:55:38,730
And we will take revenge of
Öktem Bey and our warriors.

569
00:55:41,500 --> 00:55:45,700
Mashallah! We will definitely take it.

570
00:55:45,750 --> 00:55:48,050
We will take it, Inshallah.

571
00:56:02,790 --> 00:56:03,910
Osman.

572
00:56:04,660 --> 00:56:08,010
Was this a good time for a secret search?

573
00:56:08,330 --> 00:56:09,980
This is exactly the time.

574
00:56:11,130 --> 00:56:12,800
Well, what about Nayman?

575
00:56:15,130 --> 00:56:16,860
Don't you trust your Bey?

576
00:56:17,820 --> 00:56:19,620
I certainly trust you, my dear Osman.

577
00:56:19,650 --> 00:56:21,290
You are the only one I trust.

578
00:56:21,320 --> 00:56:23,320
Don't act like you don't know.

579
00:56:24,500 --> 00:56:26,220
Thank you.

580
00:56:27,490 --> 00:56:29,490
I will be victorious, Inshallah.

581
00:56:30,140 --> 00:56:33,810
But you say what if it happened otherwise?

582
00:56:34,490 --> 00:56:35,990
Whatever happens.

583
00:56:36,180 --> 00:56:37,860
We're mortal, Malhun.

584
00:56:38,260 --> 00:56:40,660
The state will remain.

585
00:56:44,060 --> 00:56:46,940
What makes a state a state are the people.

586
00:56:52,820 --> 00:56:54,120
I want to see them.

587
00:56:55,430 --> 00:56:57,780
I want to see them, Malhun.

588
00:57:11,160 --> 00:57:12,760
Is it okay, son?

589
00:57:12,810 --> 00:57:14,810
I know who you are.

590
00:57:16,810 --> 00:57:18,560
I'm traveling, son.

591
00:57:18,830 --> 00:57:20,130
I am a traveler.

592
00:57:26,210 --> 00:57:27,540
Tell me, who am I?

593
00:57:28,260 --> 00:57:31,310
You are Osman Bey.
I don't forget the person after I see him.

594
00:57:32,280 --> 00:57:34,880
I saw you on horseback in Söğüt.

595
00:57:36,860 --> 00:57:39,320
And when I saw you fight, I made sure.

596
00:57:40,310 --> 00:57:43,810
Come see, come.

597
00:57:45,290 --> 00:57:48,990
Well, did you tell your mother
and father about me?

598
00:57:49,010 --> 00:57:50,700
Is this why the table is
in this condition?

599
00:57:50,710 --> 00:57:53,430
No, this table is like this for everyone.

600
00:57:55,590 --> 00:57:58,860
Well, what about the words
you said in the market square?

601
00:58:00,230 --> 00:58:01,980
Did you know me then?

602
00:58:02,020 --> 00:58:04,570
If I didn't know that the one standing
in front of me was Osman Bey...

603
00:58:04,600 --> 00:58:07,970
why should I even speak?

604
00:58:09,910 --> 00:58:11,260
Now...

605
00:58:12,030 --> 00:58:14,600
This will be a secret between you and me.

606
00:58:16,480 --> 00:58:19,790
- State secret.
- State secret.

607
00:58:21,270 --> 00:58:22,590
Okay.

608
00:58:23,260 --> 00:58:25,500
The table of the poor shall be like this.

609
00:58:25,570 --> 00:58:27,570
No, no.

610
00:58:27,880 --> 00:58:31,480
Mashallah, it is more beautiful
and blessed than many tables.

611
00:58:31,760 --> 00:58:33,760
Yes.

612
00:58:38,890 --> 00:58:42,950
Yenişehir/ Osman Bey's palace

613
00:59:00,245 --> 00:59:03,245
How much time is
left for iftaar, Cerkutay?

614
00:59:03,905 --> 00:59:05,195
I don't feel well.

615
00:59:05,335 --> 00:59:07,335
I don't feel well.

616
00:59:09,565 --> 00:59:11,365
Look at you.

617
00:59:11,445 --> 00:59:14,495
Look at the situation he's gotten
himself into, Ülgen Hatun.

618
00:59:17,165 --> 00:59:19,235
But you weren't saying that out there.

619
00:59:21,285 --> 00:59:24,635
Now I understand what you're doing

620
00:59:25,935 --> 00:59:27,685
You are playing on me.

621
00:59:28,740 --> 00:59:33,870
You can't hear what you're saying because
you're so hungry, Gürbüz Alp.

622
00:59:33,920 --> 00:59:35,920
But am I like that?

623
00:59:36,480 --> 00:59:38,410
Can hunger bend me?

624
00:59:38,470 --> 00:59:40,290
Isn't it, Ülgen Hatun?

625
00:59:42,500 --> 00:59:45,020
Nothing can twist
Cerkutay's wrist.

626
00:59:46,460 --> 00:59:48,450
The world knows that.

627
00:59:48,470 --> 00:59:51,990
Nothing can twist
Cerkutay's wrist.

628
00:59:59,310 --> 01:00:01,010
Ülgen.

629
01:00:02,510 --> 01:00:04,210
Your mother is here.

630
01:00:14,160 --> 01:00:15,690
Why didn't you tell me?

631
01:00:15,740 --> 01:00:17,770
I forgot about this, I forgot.

632
01:00:23,540 --> 01:00:26,110
No, man, I don't think
she heard from there.

633
01:00:27,110 --> 01:00:28,940
Right?

634
01:00:31,110 --> 01:00:32,310
She is an old woman.

635
01:00:32,590 --> 01:00:33,970
Yeah, she's old after all.

636
01:00:33,990 --> 01:00:35,990
She must not have heard.

637
01:00:39,370 --> 01:00:41,640
The dark midwife is here, too.

638
01:00:41,740 --> 01:00:43,120
What does it mean?

639
01:00:43,570 --> 01:00:45,420
Do they make the guest work?

640
01:00:47,670 --> 01:00:49,630
Who is the guest?

641
01:00:50,280 --> 01:00:54,330
What are you doing in
the kitchen, Gürbüz Alp?

642
01:00:54,400 --> 01:00:57,110
I think fasting has affected you.

643
01:00:57,420 --> 01:01:00,420
I came to set this lunatic at ease.

644
01:01:01,030 --> 01:01:04,890
No, fasting did not affect me.

645
01:01:05,170 --> 01:01:09,600
I eat a meal at suhoor that is
enough for me for ten days.

646
01:01:10,020 --> 01:01:11,990
Mashallah!

647
01:01:12,020 --> 01:01:15,270
What is this lunatic doing here?

648
01:01:19,310 --> 01:01:21,080
You lunatic.

649
01:01:27,250 --> 01:01:28,990
What do you do?

650
01:01:30,720 --> 01:01:33,310
Yes, you, what are you doing?

651
01:01:35,460 --> 01:01:36,800
Nothing.

652
01:01:37,380 --> 01:01:39,880
Come on, don't look like that, come on.

653
01:01:41,440 --> 01:01:43,140
Come on.

654
01:01:45,510 --> 01:01:46,840
Come here.

655
01:01:49,420 --> 01:01:51,230
Come here.

656
01:01:51,320 --> 01:01:54,620
Come on, get the pebbles out of these,
my eyes don't see well anymore.

657
01:01:58,240 --> 01:02:00,180
I will, mother.

658
01:02:00,600 --> 01:02:03,160
What are you doing? Give it
to me, Cerkutay.

659
01:02:03,220 --> 01:02:04,810
Let him do it.

660
01:02:06,200 --> 01:02:10,580
Isn't he crazy and standing like that
without work? Let him do it.

661
01:02:11,330 --> 01:02:13,010
He can do this.

662
01:02:14,140 --> 01:02:19,150
- You will, right?
- I will.

663
01:02:20,930 --> 01:02:23,050
Go get the cheese curd dough.

664
01:02:23,110 --> 01:02:24,810
He certainly does.

665
01:02:25,920 --> 01:02:28,420
Fits very well in his hand.

666
01:02:28,910 --> 01:02:31,410
Fits very well in his hand

667
01:02:31,440 --> 01:02:33,600
With both hands, not with one hand!

668
01:02:33,860 --> 01:02:37,130
Take it out with both hands, mix it up.

669
01:02:37,160 --> 01:02:39,180
Do it.

670
01:02:40,605 --> 01:02:43,215
They are waiting for food in the evening.

671
01:02:43,505 --> 01:02:45,045
Gürbüz Alp.

672
01:02:46,535 --> 01:02:48,805
Bring firewood for the stove.

673
01:02:49,125 --> 01:02:52,485
This lunatic wouldn't do that.

674
01:02:52,705 --> 01:02:55,405
He can't do it, he can't.

675
01:02:55,555 --> 01:02:59,175
Right, this lunatic can't do it.

676
01:03:00,400 --> 01:03:02,759
I am good at it.

677
01:03:05,880 --> 01:03:08,079
Woods to the oven...

678
01:03:08,440 --> 01:03:10,839
...and the lunatics into the fire! '

679
01:03:11,000 --> 01:03:12,559
Right, Cerkutay?

680
01:03:13,040 --> 01:03:16,999
Wooooddd...wooo...wood!

681
01:03:19,640 --> 01:03:22,639
You'll see, you'll...

682
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:33,119
Here, have some.
You can't work with an empty stomach.

683
01:03:34,120 --> 01:03:37,759
No, Cerkutay is fasting,
he doesn't want to eat!

684
01:03:38,000 --> 01:03:40,119
Lunatics don't fast!

685
01:03:40,280 --> 01:03:42,959
They just don't!

686
01:03:43,200 --> 01:03:44,439
I'm fasting!

687
01:03:44,600 --> 01:03:45,519
Fasting!

688
01:03:53,240 --> 01:03:54,479
Girl!

689
01:03:56,320 --> 01:03:59,919
Why does that lunatic keep following you?

690
01:04:00,200 --> 01:04:02,799
He even brought you red cloth!

691
01:04:08,200 --> 01:04:09,599
Esma!

692
01:04:10,120 --> 01:04:12,919
We forgot to add salt!
I'll get the salt!

693
01:04:13,280 --> 01:04:14,009
The salt!

694
01:04:14,009 --> 01:04:16,879
What made you think
that you could fool me?

695
01:04:19,400 --> 01:04:20,679
Go on!

696
01:04:22,160 --> 01:04:24,759
Well, I will make you pay.

697
01:04:25,200 --> 01:04:29,199
What made you think
that you could fool the Dark Midwife?

698
01:04:29,440 --> 01:04:33,119
You don't even half the experience I have!

699
01:04:41,880 --> 01:04:44,399
In the Name of Allah,
the Most Compassionate, the most Merciful

700
01:04:44,480 --> 01:04:46,440
-In the Name of Allah,
the Most Compassionate, the most Merciful

701
01:04:46,440 --> 01:04:47,440
Allah bless you.

702
01:04:47,440 --> 01:04:48,159
Amen.

703
01:04:49,440 --> 01:04:50,239
Let's eat.

704
01:04:50,760 --> 01:04:51,959
Thank you.

705
01:04:52,200 --> 01:04:53,919
Here you go.

706
01:04:56,640 --> 01:04:58,239
Here, son.

707
01:05:02,160 --> 01:05:04,559
In the Name of Allah,
the Most Compassionate, the most Merciful

708
01:05:13,400 --> 01:05:15,810
May Allah give you prosperity.

709
01:05:15,810 --> 01:05:19,639
Ali Aga, you did not have to prepare
such a table in a hard time like this.

710
01:05:20,920 --> 01:05:23,319
As Prophet PBUH said...

711
01:05:23,640 --> 01:05:26,679
...if a Muslim feeds another
hungry Muslim...

712
01:05:26,920 --> 01:05:30,839
...Allah will feed that Muslim
with fruits in His heaven.

713
01:05:31,280 --> 01:05:34,039
We have no hope left
in this world, my Bey.

714
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:40,559
It's enough for us if
we can have fruits in the afterlife.

715
01:05:41,560 --> 01:05:44,199
Thank you, thank you, but...

716
01:05:45,320 --> 01:05:48,999
...you can't just forget about this world
and focus on the fruits of the afterlife.

717
01:05:49,600 --> 01:05:52,999
You have a son made of steel.
The future is theirs.

718
01:05:53,320 --> 01:05:56,559
You won't leave this world without
planting a tree for them.

719
01:05:56,760 --> 01:05:59,639
Muslims shouldn't fall into despair,
that's why...

720
01:06:00,080 --> 01:06:04,559
...we will always stand together and
overcome these troubles, with the help of Allah.

721
01:06:04,680 --> 01:06:06,159
I hope so.

722
01:06:07,720 --> 01:06:10,319
So tell me...

723
01:06:14,600 --> 01:06:19,079
These bandits, do they always bother you?

724
01:06:20,560 --> 01:06:22,119
Always.

725
01:06:26,440 --> 01:06:29,319
A brave man will always...

726
01:06:29,840 --> 01:06:32,759
...stand against the oppressors
in these lands.

727
01:06:34,200 --> 01:06:40,919
You will leave, but we have been
in these lands for years.

728
01:06:41,760 --> 01:06:44,959
If we laugh one day, we cry for another 3.

729
01:06:49,120 --> 01:06:55,119
All Aga, you know the best,
but those tears..

730
01:06:55,560 --> 01:06:59,239
...might become water for a tree
you are going to plant for your children.

731
01:06:59,240 --> 01:07:01,839
Maybe that brave man is your son.

732
01:07:08,560 --> 01:07:11,319
We can't understand words with such wisdom, my lady.

733
01:07:11,560 --> 01:07:15,679
But you are saying that there is
a purpose in the pain I suffer.

734
01:07:21,000 --> 01:07:21,999
Ali Aga.

735
01:07:24,360 --> 01:07:26,879
Your furnitures are missing.

736
01:07:32,120 --> 01:07:35,159
I couldn't say it when
we were with the blacksmith.

737
01:07:35,840 --> 01:07:38,719
His coin is not enough for the rent.

738
01:07:39,120 --> 01:07:41,599
We keep helping each other.

739
01:07:46,880 --> 01:07:50,479
As long as you support each other...

740
01:07:50,800 --> 01:07:53,719
...with the help of Allah,
we can't be defeated.

741
01:08:06,320 --> 01:08:08,839
Damascus.

742
01:08:08,840 --> 01:08:11,599
Talay's Secret Base

743
01:09:07,479 --> 01:09:08,879
Merchant.

744
01:09:08,920 --> 01:09:09,799
Yes.

745
01:09:10,040 --> 01:09:12,999
Too crowded for a merchant.

746
01:09:14,080 --> 01:09:14,919
Why?

747
01:09:15,800 --> 01:09:19,999
The relic we are carrying is
more valuable than anything.

748
01:09:20,840 --> 01:09:23,559
We don't want to witness Nayman's wrath.

749
01:09:38,840 --> 01:09:42,479
If this is fake..

750
01:09:43,160 --> 01:09:46,238
...then you will witness my wrath.

751
01:09:51,279 --> 01:09:52,599
Aren't you afraid?

752
01:09:53,279 --> 01:09:55,639
I am afraid.

753
01:09:56,280 --> 01:09:58,359
But I also ask the reason.

754
01:09:59,120 --> 01:10:01,519
If he wanted to kill me...

755
01:10:01,960 --> 01:10:05,759
...why did Nayman allow
me to go all this way?

756
01:10:06,920 --> 01:10:09,279
He could have killed me right then.

757
01:10:12,040 --> 01:10:13,439
You're right.

758
01:10:19,760 --> 01:10:22,799
Nayman always takes precautions.

759
01:10:24,360 --> 01:10:28,599
The letter describes the appearance
of the merchant.

760
01:10:37,000 --> 01:10:38,559
Allah is the Greatest.

761
01:10:41,080 --> 01:10:44,119
Allah hears whoever praises Him.

762
01:10:48,040 --> 01:10:49,839
Allah is the Greatest.

763
01:10:57,000 --> 01:10:58,679
Allah is the Greatest.

764
01:11:03,360 --> 01:11:04,959
Allah is the Greatest.

765
01:11:08,240 --> 01:11:10,919
Allah is the Greatest.

766
01:11:18,920 --> 01:11:21,239
Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy.

767
01:11:22,400 --> 01:11:24,679
Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy.

768
01:11:37,000 --> 01:11:40,479
Nayman said a gold bar was enough.

769
01:11:41,200 --> 01:11:42,359
Is that right?

770
01:11:42,360 --> 01:11:43,759
Not enough.

771
01:11:47,000 --> 01:11:49,839
Pretty enough I think.

772
01:12:00,440 --> 01:12:02,679
Open the door!

773
01:12:04,400 --> 01:12:06,599
You have something that belongs to us.

774
01:12:07,440 --> 01:12:08,879
Where's the seal?

775
01:12:10,200 --> 01:12:13,799
I won't ask again.
Where's Cengiz Khan's seal?

776
01:12:13,800 --> 01:12:17,199
I won’t tell you even if you kill me!

777
01:12:17,960 --> 01:12:20,079
I'll take the seal eventually.

778
01:12:20,360 --> 01:12:22,519
With or without you.

779
01:12:24,240 --> 01:12:25,279
Wait.

780
01:12:52,160 --> 01:12:53,149
Tell me Mongol.

781
01:12:53,880 --> 01:12:55,839
Are you on his side or not?

782
01:12:55,840 --> 01:12:57,319
Who are you?

783
01:12:57,320 --> 01:12:59,319
I'm here in the name of Gazan Khan.

784
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:01,319
Who are you?

785
01:13:07,040 --> 01:13:12,439
I am Commander Turgut Bey who serves
the ruler of the borders, Osman Bey.

786
01:13:16,760 --> 01:13:20,519
Sultan Alaeddin sent a letter to
Gazan Khan.

787
01:13:21,480 --> 01:13:25,159
He told us about Osman Bey and you.

788
01:13:25,920 --> 01:13:29,159
He said Talay and Nayman will rebel.

789
01:13:29,840 --> 01:13:31,919
I came to see it myself.

790
01:13:32,920 --> 01:13:34,479
I guess...

791
01:13:34,880 --> 01:13:36,839
...the letter was true.

792
01:13:39,800 --> 01:13:42,639
So Bala Hatun fulfilled her duty.

793
01:13:43,480 --> 01:13:44,639
Good.

794
01:13:46,440 --> 01:13:47,439
Good.

795
01:13:48,320 --> 01:13:50,359
If your words are true...

796
01:13:50,600 --> 01:13:52,359
...now the rest will be taken care of us.

797
01:13:53,000 --> 01:13:54,359
Still, what we need...

798
01:13:55,320 --> 01:13:57,479
...is Cengiz Khan's seal...

799
01:13:58,680 --> 01:14:00,479
He's a Mongol.

800
01:14:01,040 --> 01:14:03,639
It won't take long to find what he hid.

801
01:14:23,480 --> 01:14:25,359
In the Name of Allah,
the Most Compassionate, the most Merciful

802
01:14:29,400 --> 01:14:31,559
Allah bless you my Bey.

803
01:14:31,680 --> 01:14:33,919
May our fight be blessed my Bey.

804
01:14:33,920 --> 01:14:35,559
May Allah bless you my Bey.

805
01:14:39,080 --> 01:14:40,399
Thank you.

806
01:14:41,240 --> 01:14:42,959
Thank you. Thank you.

807
01:14:44,160 --> 01:14:46,159
-May Allah bless you.
-Thank you.

808
01:14:54,600 --> 01:14:56,399
-Konur.
-Yes my Bey?

809
01:14:57,200 --> 01:14:59,119
Bring the ink and paper.

810
01:14:59,680 --> 01:15:01,119
And you go back to the mansion.

811
01:15:02,440 --> 01:15:03,679
As you wish my Bey.

812
01:15:04,600 --> 01:15:06,759
Alaeddin. Orhan.

813
01:15:07,360 --> 01:15:08,959
You stay with me.

814
01:15:20,560 --> 01:15:21,919
My sheikh.

815
01:15:21,920 --> 01:15:24,359
Take a seat.

816
01:15:33,160 --> 01:15:35,999
Today I've walked among our people...

817
01:15:35,999 --> 01:15:38,639
...in disguise of a public man.

818
01:15:40,440 --> 01:15:42,959
But what I've seen...

819
01:15:43,480 --> 01:15:45,759
...both made me sad...

820
01:15:47,320 --> 01:15:49,199
...and lessened my hope.

821
01:15:49,200 --> 01:15:49,839
...and optimistic.

822
01:15:50,040 --> 01:15:52,639
What did you see my Bey?

823
01:15:52,960 --> 01:15:55,999
Tradesmen don't have any business left.

824
01:15:56,600 --> 01:15:59,630
While they can't even buy and sell,

825
01:15:59,630 --> 01:16:01,459
Like everything was going okay...

826
01:16:01,459 --> 01:16:03,239
...they're expected to pay rent.

827
01:16:08,160 --> 01:16:10,159
Tell me.

828
01:16:11,680 --> 01:16:13,319
What should we do sons?

829
01:16:14,520 --> 01:16:16,399
While there are
such tough wars going on...

830
01:16:16,720 --> 01:16:20,319
...those whoever are after money
should pay for it my bey.

831
01:16:21,480 --> 01:16:25,059
The one who worries about their
wealth in this time shall lose their life.

832
01:16:29,120 --> 01:16:31,359
During these times, my bey...

833
01:16:31,360 --> 01:16:33,799
...we should look at the bigger picture.

834
01:16:34,800 --> 01:16:40,279
Those people might just have the rent
as their income, as the trade won't work.

835
01:16:44,760 --> 01:16:48,279
Are we going to protect the landlord
and disregard the tradesmen, brother?

836
01:16:49,640 --> 01:16:51,439
I don't mean that.

837
01:16:51,440 --> 01:16:53,239
A middle ground.

838
01:16:55,600 --> 01:16:58,139
The tradesmen will declare their income.

839
01:16:58,800 --> 01:17:02,799
And the landlord will decide the rent accordingly.

840
01:17:06,080 --> 01:17:09,679
Expecting the amount of money that
the merchant barely earns...

841
01:17:09,680 --> 01:17:11,999
...would be the end of the people.

842
01:17:16,520 --> 01:17:18,519
So you're saying...

843
01:17:20,040 --> 01:17:22,239
...while one struggle...

844
01:17:22,240 --> 01:17:24,559
...the other won't be at ease.

845
01:17:27,640 --> 01:17:30,679
Everyone will work together, you say.

846
01:17:34,680 --> 01:17:37,999
The tradesmen's income will be proven too.

847
01:17:38,000 --> 01:17:40,679
It won't be open to any misuse.

848
01:17:43,520 --> 01:17:45,159
My sheikh...

849
01:17:47,240 --> 01:17:49,319
...you heard them.

850
01:17:49,320 --> 01:17:51,399
What do you think?

851
01:17:54,040 --> 01:17:57,319
The student has surpassed the teacher,
Osman Bey.

852
01:17:58,400 --> 01:18:01,319
They didn't leave anything else to say.

853
01:18:02,400 --> 01:18:07,039
Both Orhan and Alaeddin
are right about what they've said.

854
01:18:09,160 --> 01:18:10,599
But..

855
01:18:11,120 --> 01:18:12,959
...what's important is...

856
01:18:12,960 --> 01:18:15,199
...to find a middle ground.

857
01:18:17,320 --> 01:18:19,959
And for that..

858
01:18:19,960 --> 01:18:22,999
...two sides, just like your sons here...

859
01:18:23,000 --> 01:18:26,439
...should come together.

860
01:18:29,760 --> 01:18:32,119
..we'll find a middle ground.

861
01:18:35,840 --> 01:18:37,479
Thank you my sheikh.

862
01:18:38,280 --> 01:18:39,679
Thank you.

863
01:18:40,400 --> 01:18:42,399
Take the pen.

864
01:18:45,640 --> 01:18:47,079
Write down.

865
01:18:47,640 --> 01:18:49,839
It's Osman Bey's law.

866
01:18:50,800 --> 01:18:53,439
After the 20th of Ramadan...

867
01:18:55,120 --> 01:18:58,359
...the amount of money
tradesmen earn will be counted.

868
01:18:59,200 --> 01:19:01,799
And everyone will...

869
01:19:02,240 --> 01:19:04,919
...give their rent accordingly to it.

870
01:19:09,440 --> 01:19:12,399
If someone lies about their income...

871
01:19:12,920 --> 01:19:15,199
...then they will...

872
01:19:15,200 --> 01:19:17,879
...pay the price for it.

873
01:19:21,440 --> 01:19:22,639
They will...

874
01:19:24,120 --> 01:19:26,649
...be judged for earning haram money.

875
01:19:27,360 --> 01:19:29,719
After every 20th of the each month...

876
01:19:29,880 --> 01:19:31,999
...a statement will be taken from both sides...

877
01:19:33,400 --> 01:19:36,239
...and they always will be checked.

878
01:19:41,080 --> 01:19:43,879
From now in it's Osman Bey's law.

879
01:19:45,400 --> 01:19:46,759
It will be applied.

880
01:19:55,200 --> 01:19:56,439
My sheikh.

881
01:20:12,520 --> 01:20:15,719
I'm being called lunatic now!

882
01:20:18,280 --> 01:20:21,279
The Dark Midwife hates me, too...

883
01:20:22,520 --> 01:20:25,199
What am I going to do now?

884
01:20:27,240 --> 01:20:28,759
Perhaps I should...

885
01:20:29,160 --> 01:20:30,839
...go up to her...

886
01:20:31,640 --> 01:20:33,119
...and say that...

887
01:20:33,160 --> 01:20:35,679
..."Hatun Hatun I'm not lunatic!"...

888
01:20:46,040 --> 01:20:47,639
I should say that...

889
01:20:49,880 --> 01:20:52,159
Say that...
that I...

890
01:20:52,520 --> 01:20:56,119
...that I have feelings for your
daughter Ulgen.

891
01:21:03,320 --> 01:21:05,439
I can't do that either.

892
01:21:06,000 --> 01:21:09,399
She thinks that I'm lunatic
but she's more lunatic than me.

893
01:21:11,120 --> 01:21:14,639
She will do much more
than just hitting me on the head.

894
01:21:15,320 --> 01:21:17,399
What am I going to do?

895
01:21:18,280 --> 01:21:22,199
What am I going to do?

896
01:21:26,880 --> 01:21:29,039
I'm going to make her like me.

897
01:21:34,720 --> 01:21:37,009
But she even likes Gurbuz
more than she likes me.

898
01:21:40,200 --> 01:21:42,199
Are you waiting for Suhoor, lunatic boy?

899
01:21:51,120 --> 01:21:54,159
You're the only lunatic person
I know that fasts.

900
01:21:57,120 --> 01:21:58,999
I'm half lunatic

901
01:21:59,560 --> 01:22:02,959
How can a lunatic be half lunatic?

902
01:22:03,040 --> 01:22:05,559
You either need to be completely
insane or completely sane.

903
01:22:06,040 --> 01:22:08,879
Dealing in halves
will not do any good to you.

904
01:22:11,080 --> 01:22:13,599
Now...

905
01:22:13,920 --> 01:22:17,879
...since you're half insane
and half sane...

906
01:22:18,920 --> 01:22:19,999
Yes.

907
01:22:20,600 --> 01:22:22,879
You're going to help me.

908
01:22:25,720 --> 01:22:28,759
What do you want from the lunatic?

909
01:22:29,160 --> 01:22:30,919
I want a groom.

910
01:22:31,640 --> 01:22:32,839
What?

911
01:22:33,560 --> 01:22:36,479
I said that I wanted a groom,
can't you hear?

912
01:22:39,560 --> 01:22:41,279
For whom?

913
01:22:41,920 --> 01:22:42,739
For you?

914
01:22:42,739 --> 01:22:44,999
You lunatic, stop the nonsense!

915
01:22:45,440 --> 01:22:48,519
I'd give you a nice beating
now if you weren't crazy.

916
01:22:50,800 --> 01:22:53,279
For whom do you think?

917
01:22:54,120 --> 01:22:55,999
For my daughter.

918
01:23:01,840 --> 01:23:03,079
Watch out!

919
01:23:03,840 --> 01:23:05,399
Watch out!

920
01:23:06,200 --> 01:23:09,759
So you're going to help me.

921
01:23:12,080 --> 01:23:13,919
A brave..

922
01:23:14,320 --> 01:23:17,319
...very smart...

923
01:23:18,520 --> 01:23:21,679
I said smart, alright? Not lunatic.

924
01:23:22,400 --> 01:23:23,559
Valiant...

925
01:23:23,800 --> 01:23:25,279
...really strong...

926
01:23:27,240 --> 01:23:31,359
That's the husband you're going to
find for my daughter.

927
01:23:32,960 --> 01:23:37,039
This is a kind of man Ulgen deserves.

928
01:23:41,360 --> 01:23:43,639
Watch out!

929
01:23:47,640 --> 01:23:50,439
So you are in love...

930
01:23:50,760 --> 01:23:53,759
...with my daughter, lunatic boy...

931
01:23:55,120 --> 01:23:59,519
Then you're about to
go through a tough test.

932
01:24:03,760 --> 01:24:06,439
In the Name of Allah,
the Most Compassionate, the most Merciful

933
01:24:11,520 --> 01:24:12,639
Thank you.

934
01:24:13,400 --> 01:24:15,639
Do you know Hizir PBUH?

935
01:24:17,280 --> 01:24:20,759
But don't you call me Hizir, Turgut Bey.

936
01:24:21,280 --> 01:24:23,639
People might expect miracles from me.

937
01:24:26,960 --> 01:24:31,519
We keep asking you how you
found Genghis Khan's seal..

938
01:24:32,320 --> 01:24:34,079
...but you don't tell us anything.

939
01:24:34,280 --> 01:24:36,639
How do we know if you're
really not full of miracles?

940
01:24:36,680 --> 01:24:39,559
My name is neither Hizir nor
I can do any miracles.

941
01:24:39,920 --> 01:24:42,239
I'm just a Mongol
who's been honored with Islam.

942
01:24:42,360 --> 01:24:45,079
-That's the secret to it.
-Eyvallah.

943
01:24:48,200 --> 01:24:50,519
It's about being well-protected.

944
01:24:53,160 --> 01:24:54,799
Anyway...

945
01:24:54,800 --> 01:24:57,199
...we shouldn’t give you further trouble.

946
01:24:57,640 --> 01:25:00,559
Knowing that you're safe is enough.

947
01:25:00,600 --> 01:25:02,319
Thank Allah that...

948
01:25:02,440 --> 01:25:06,559
...the mission I was given included
Suhoor with such brave men.

949
01:25:06,720 --> 01:25:07,959
Thank you.

950
01:25:08,120 --> 01:25:10,999
Thank you, as well.
It's an honor to share a meal with you.

951
01:25:13,720 --> 01:25:16,119
Alps, let's finish Suhoor...

952
01:25:16,280 --> 01:25:19,519
...and we will
hit the road after the morning prayer.

953
01:25:19,760 --> 01:25:21,279
We will first pick up Bayindir...

954
01:25:21,320 --> 01:25:24,599
... and then, if Allah permits,
our destination is Yenisehir.

955
01:25:24,880 --> 01:25:27,159
Okay, my Bey.

956
01:25:29,160 --> 01:25:30,879
Turgut Bey and his men...

957
01:25:31,160 --> 01:25:34,759
...are on a mission
beyond the borders of Seljuk.

958
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:40,559
They must have obtained
Genghis Khan's seal by now.

959
01:25:41,120 --> 01:25:43,599
They have crossed a tough road, my Bey.

960
01:25:43,840 --> 01:25:46,719
They did, they actually did.

961
01:25:47,360 --> 01:25:48,599
But..

962
01:25:49,280 --> 01:25:51,159
...this is such a seal that...

963
01:25:56,120 --> 01:26:00,439
...it is strong enough to gather all
the Mongolian Beys under one flag.

964
01:26:00,880 --> 01:26:05,119
If Nayman and Talay gets
their hands on it...

965
01:26:06,480 --> 01:26:11,559
...then they will want to remove
Muslims from these lands.

966
01:26:14,720 --> 01:26:18,559
My Bey, the seal will weaken Nayman
when we have it.

967
01:26:18,880 --> 01:26:21,079
But what strength will it bring to us?

968
01:26:21,360 --> 01:26:24,959
If we lose it and they have it...

969
01:26:25,040 --> 01:26:26,879
Don't say that, my Bey.

970
01:26:29,120 --> 01:26:30,559
Fortunetaly...

971
01:26:32,200 --> 01:26:36,879
...Bala Hatun went to Sultan Alaeddin,
and wrote a letter to Gazan Khan.

972
01:26:38,440 --> 01:26:43,039
Thanks to this letter, a Mongol commander
will come here with Turgut Bey.

973
01:26:43,280 --> 01:26:44,999
He'll have the seal.

974
01:26:45,080 --> 01:26:48,039
That Commander will stop Nayman.

975
01:26:52,040 --> 01:26:54,279
We killed them in Konya.

976
01:26:54,280 --> 01:26:57,239
If Allah permits,
we'll end them in our lands as well, my Bey.

977
01:26:57,240 --> 01:26:58,719
For sure.

978
01:26:59,320 --> 01:27:00,919
For sure, we will.

979
01:27:01,320 --> 01:27:02,439
Turan.

980
01:27:03,880 --> 01:27:05,719
What's the situation in the field?

981
01:27:05,720 --> 01:27:08,479
My Bey. There is no traps.
The field is flat.

982
01:27:08,480 --> 01:27:11,119
Both sides have the same advantage.

983
01:27:13,280 --> 01:27:15,079
Did you find the base?

984
01:27:15,080 --> 01:27:17,079
Their locations are known, my Bey.

985
01:27:17,120 --> 01:27:20,279
Then sent Alps there at sunrise.

986
01:27:20,440 --> 01:27:23,359
When they move, alps will attack.

987
01:27:23,600 --> 01:27:25,239
As you wish my Bey.

988
01:27:26,280 --> 01:27:27,919
Now...

989
01:27:29,920 --> 01:27:32,639
...eat well in Suhoor tonight.

990
01:27:33,400 --> 01:27:37,199
Tomorrow, the biggest war this land
has ever seen will come to life.

991
01:27:43,400 --> 01:27:45,319
My Bey.

992
01:27:47,760 --> 01:27:49,319
What about us?

993
01:27:49,920 --> 01:27:51,519
Sons...

994
01:27:53,240 --> 01:27:56,079
...you have a different mission.

995
01:28:05,360 --> 01:28:08,959
You will guard the bazaar
according to Osman Bey's order.

996
01:28:08,960 --> 01:28:11,319
We won't let those bandits make a move.

997
01:28:11,320 --> 01:28:12,639
As you wish my Bey.

998
01:28:12,640 --> 01:28:13,879
Come on.

999
01:28:22,640 --> 01:28:23,359
Come.

1000
01:28:30,720 --> 01:28:32,599
Peace be with you, Ali Aga.

1001
01:28:32,600 --> 01:28:34,399
Peace be upon you too.

1002
01:28:34,400 --> 01:28:36,839
The shop is now yours.

1003
01:28:37,240 --> 01:28:40,159
Osman Bey has bought
the shop in your name.

1004
01:28:40,160 --> 01:28:42,159
Enjoy it!

1005
01:28:43,080 --> 01:28:44,799
Osman Bey?

1006
01:28:50,960 --> 01:28:53,399
-Have a good day.
-Thank you.

1007
01:29:02,040 --> 01:29:04,479
Hear me out!
Hear me out!

1008
01:29:11,720 --> 01:29:13,639
Osman Bey's new law commands...

1009
01:29:13,800 --> 01:29:16,879
...that after the the 20th day of Ramadan..

1010
01:29:26,400 --> 01:29:30,599
The law will help the traders
get back on their feet!

1011
01:29:31,240 --> 01:29:32,479
Indeed.

1012
01:29:32,840 --> 01:29:35,519
And once we defeat Nayman...

1013
01:29:36,040 --> 01:29:38,769
...both the tradesmen and the trading
will come to life.

1014
01:29:42,640 --> 01:29:46,199
Let’s not keep the ones
who are in need waiting, my Beys.

1015
01:29:46,680 --> 01:29:49,319
There are still many
houses we need to visit.

1016
01:30:02,400 --> 01:30:05,039
Yenisehir, Osman Bey's Mansion.

1017
01:30:07,600 --> 01:30:08,799
Osman.

1018
01:30:10,480 --> 01:30:14,919
Nayman has tried to trap you before,
using Orhan.

1019
01:30:16,360 --> 01:30:19,639
He will try to do something
shady in this fight too.

1020
01:30:21,840 --> 01:30:23,759
Do you think that
he will cheat again?

1021
01:30:23,840 --> 01:30:27,399
I do, my Bala.
He'll definitely cheat again.

1022
01:30:28,800 --> 01:30:33,079
You know he cheats yet you accept
his duel invitation!

1023
01:30:33,240 --> 01:30:35,119
He trusts his cheats.

1024
01:30:35,520 --> 01:30:38,959
But I trust my Allah first,
then to my own strength.

1025
01:30:39,320 --> 01:30:42,439
May Allah make their plans fail, my Bey.

1026
01:30:43,160 --> 01:30:44,879
Be cautious.

1027
01:30:45,040 --> 01:30:46,439
Amen, Bala.

1028
01:30:47,760 --> 01:30:49,679
Amen, my dear.

1029
01:30:50,280 --> 01:30:54,599
Bala, until now, you have always
supported my dream.

1030
01:30:55,280 --> 01:30:56,839
Thank you.

1031
01:30:58,160 --> 01:30:59,999
Give me your blessings.

1032
01:31:02,520 --> 01:31:04,399
If I fall...

1033
01:31:05,120 --> 01:31:06,159
...keep my dream alive.

1034
01:31:06,360 --> 01:31:08,479
What does that mean, Osman?

1035
01:31:10,480 --> 01:31:14,279
I give you my blessing, but may Allah
not allow you to be defeated.

1036
01:31:14,920 --> 01:31:18,239
May He let you live long enough to see
your dream come true with your children.

1037
01:31:18,800 --> 01:31:20,119
Amen.

1038
01:31:35,800 --> 01:31:38,319
Look what Bayindir did!

1039
01:31:39,520 --> 01:31:42,199
Look what that dog did!

1040
01:31:43,400 --> 01:31:46,359
He played some tricks again, and escaped!

1041
01:31:47,400 --> 01:31:49,839
My Bey, forgive us, we just...

1042
01:31:49,840 --> 01:31:51,639
You just what?

1043
01:31:55,440 --> 01:31:59,039
All you had to do was to keep an eye on
a man tied to a tree!

1044
01:32:00,760 --> 01:32:02,319
What have you done?

1045
01:32:03,160 --> 01:32:05,839
Tell me, how did he escape?

1046
01:32:07,440 --> 01:32:10,079
What were you doing?

1047
01:32:13,680 --> 01:32:16,159
I will ask about this again in Yenisehir..

1048
01:32:20,720 --> 01:32:23,439
But I will make Bayindir pay for this.

1049
01:32:23,680 --> 01:32:27,039
Even if he asks for forgiveness,
I will not forgive him!

1050
01:32:28,840 --> 01:32:30,999
I will turn his life into hell!

1051
01:32:33,880 --> 01:32:34,759
Tell me, is there any traces?

1052
01:32:34,840 --> 01:32:38,719
My Bey, there is a river on this side,
there are traces over there.

1053
01:32:38,720 --> 01:32:40,879
It looks like they went that way.

1054
01:32:43,560 --> 01:32:45,759
What’s on your mind, Turgut Bey?

1055
01:32:49,040 --> 01:32:51,599
We got what we want from Bayindir, but...

1056
01:32:51,760 --> 01:32:54,719
...if he reaches Nayman before us...

1057
01:32:55,400 --> 01:32:57,999
...then all or plans will be for nothing.

1058
01:33:00,160 --> 01:33:02,199
We need to go quickly.

1059
01:33:02,840 --> 01:33:04,439
Quickly! Come on alps!

1060
01:33:04,760 --> 01:33:06,519
We will ride for homeland!

1061
01:33:06,600 --> 01:33:08,479
We won't stop to rest!

1062
01:33:08,640 --> 01:33:13,559
If Osman Bey doesn't learn about this in time,
we won't have a homeland we can return!

1063
01:33:13,720 --> 01:33:14,799
Come on!

1064
01:33:24,920 --> 01:33:26,239
Come on!

1065
01:33:28,200 --> 01:33:28,999
Come on!

1066
01:33:40,920 --> 01:33:43,759
My Bey is coming, be quick alps!

1067
01:33:50,240 --> 01:33:51,599
Brothers!

1068
01:33:52,200 --> 01:33:55,479
Our weapons will be drenched
in Mongolian blood today.

1069
01:34:05,000 --> 01:34:09,079
Today is Nayman's last day, I can feel it.

1070
01:34:28,200 --> 01:34:29,799
Brothers!

1071
01:34:31,880 --> 01:34:38,039
May your swords be sharp, may your spears
be strong, and your hearts brave!

1072
01:35:22,080 --> 01:35:22,879
Alps.

1073
01:35:27,200 --> 01:35:29,599
Today I made a deal with Nayman.

1074
01:35:30,750 --> 01:35:32,279
We will battle.

1075
01:35:33,960 --> 01:35:35,519
As the name implies...

1076
01:35:35,560 --> 01:35:38,759
This field is called men's field!

1077
01:35:41,200 --> 01:35:44,119
We don't know what Nayman
ordered his warriors.

1078
01:35:44,840 --> 01:35:46,279
But you...

1079
01:35:46,760 --> 01:35:49,959
...you will never give up on your duty.

1080
01:35:50,640 --> 01:35:55,879
Today we will bury Nayman
and his army in this land.

1081
01:35:55,880 --> 01:35:57,879
Okay my Bey.

1082
01:35:58,600 --> 01:35:59,879
For sure, my Bey!

1083
01:36:00,720 --> 01:36:01,879
Now listen to me.

1084
01:36:03,240 --> 01:36:04,399
For sure...

1085
01:36:05,440 --> 01:36:07,199
For sure, our plan is decent.

1086
01:36:08,640 --> 01:36:09,679
But.

1087
01:36:10,320 --> 01:36:12,879
...if things don't go the way we want...

1088
01:36:14,480 --> 01:36:15,919
...and fate...

1089
01:36:17,720 --> 01:36:19,919
...has decided I become a martyr...

1090
01:36:20,320 --> 01:36:24,039
...don't be frightened and turn back on your duty.

1091
01:36:25,320 --> 01:36:27,999
You will destroy those bases.

1092
01:36:28,680 --> 01:36:31,399
You will protect the people.

1093
01:36:34,360 --> 01:36:36,279
Even if I fall a martyr...

1094
01:36:37,240 --> 01:36:38,119
...that Nayman...

1095
01:36:39,040 --> 01:36:41,359
...won't leave this land alive!

1096
01:36:44,360 --> 01:36:46,319
And the last thing he hears will be...

1097
01:36:50,280 --> 01:36:57,159
Allah is the Greatest!

1098
01:36:57,640 --> 01:36:59,599
Allah is the Greatest!

1099
01:37:01,760 --> 01:37:02,599
My Bey.

1100
01:37:03,000 --> 01:37:06,679
Kargun tribe's Alps are in position waiting for you.

1101
01:37:10,280 --> 01:37:12,159
.Why are we waiting Aktemur?

1102
01:37:12,160 --> 01:37:14,159
Let’s leave.

1103
01:37:19,040 --> 01:37:20,279
My Bey, people approaching.

1104
01:37:24,320 --> 01:37:26,399
I won’t let you leave.

1105
01:37:29,600 --> 01:37:31,719
Are they here to stop us Aktemur?

1106
01:37:31,760 --> 01:37:33,159
Is there something wrong?

1107
01:37:43,640 --> 01:37:44,839
We were waiting for you.

1108
01:37:55,640 --> 01:37:57,519
I sat on the post as you wished.

1109
01:37:58,200 --> 01:38:00,159
Thank you my nephew.

1110
01:38:00,400 --> 01:38:01,639
But...

1111
01:38:02,080 --> 01:38:04,439
...you kicked me out of the assembly...

1112
01:38:04,440 --> 01:38:06,159
...they think I'm the enemy.

1113
01:38:06,160 --> 01:38:07,679
Let them.

1114
01:38:07,800 --> 01:38:11,359
Let them so that th enemy can find you.

1115
01:38:12,240 --> 01:38:14,319
Mother Sultan and the others..

1116
01:38:14,720 --> 01:38:16,319
...those who are secretly enemies...

1117
01:38:16,880 --> 01:38:19,039
...might come to you now.

1118
01:38:20,080 --> 01:38:21,039
Thank you my Bey.

1119
01:38:21,760 --> 01:38:23,319
What's my next duty?

1120
01:38:23,680 --> 01:38:25,719
Your next duty...

1121
01:38:28,960 --> 01:38:30,239
...is...

1122
01:38:30,760 --> 01:38:31,999
...Marmaracik.

1123
01:38:34,840 --> 01:38:36,479
You'll take Marmaracik.

1124
01:38:38,920 --> 01:38:41,999
Nayman must have heard you betrayed me.

1125
01:38:42,040 --> 01:38:43,999
He'll think I'm alone now.

1126
01:38:44,000 --> 01:38:48,039
When I start the battle with him,
Marmaracik...

1127
01:38:48,680 --> 01:38:50,039
....will be defenseless.

1128
01:38:52,560 --> 01:38:54,799
He won't think we'll attack there.

1129
01:38:56,760 --> 01:38:57,759
Son.

1130
01:39:01,760 --> 01:39:04,359
For the blood of the soldier
whose post you sit on.

1131
01:39:07,440 --> 01:39:09,399
Do it for Oktem Bey.

1132
01:39:14,120 --> 01:39:15,759
As you wish my Bey.

1133
01:39:15,880 --> 01:39:18,719
Kargun's soldiers have been waiting for this.

1134
01:39:19,080 --> 01:39:22,519
Allah is with us. Victory is ours.

1135
01:39:22,960 --> 01:39:24,799
Go in peace son.

1136
01:39:28,080 --> 01:39:29,759
Sisters, let's go.

1137
01:39:43,280 --> 01:39:45,679
Osman Bey sends his regards Aktemur.

1138
01:39:45,680 --> 01:39:47,039
Peace be upon him.

1139
01:39:47,400 --> 01:39:50,279
These are yours.
Mongol warriors' clothes.

1140
01:39:56,480 --> 01:39:58,719
Tell me Aktemur Bey.

1141
01:39:59,040 --> 01:40:02,879
Why didn't you tell us
you spoke to your uncle?

1142
01:40:05,960 --> 01:40:07,759
It’s my duty mother.

1143
01:40:08,040 --> 01:40:09,479
Don't be down about it.

1144
01:40:09,480 --> 01:40:12,159
No one but my uncle knows.

1145
01:40:14,920 --> 01:40:18,679
So Osman Bey knew you
were going to be sit on the throne.

1146
01:40:20,800 --> 01:40:22,759
But I don't get it.

1147
01:40:22,760 --> 01:40:24,839
Why did you not reveal it?

1148
01:40:24,840 --> 01:40:26,999
My uncle doesn't trust Ismihan.

1149
01:40:27,000 --> 01:40:29,839
Thinks she will stab us in the back
the first chance she gets.

1150
01:40:31,800 --> 01:40:35,239
Mother Sultan would want to use my mother
and you the first chance she gets.

1151
01:40:37,200 --> 01:40:38,799
Don't be mad Alcicek.

1152
01:40:38,800 --> 01:40:40,159
Of course I won't.

1153
01:40:40,160 --> 01:40:42,399
You thought well.

1154
01:40:48,280 --> 01:40:49,639
Now...

1155
01:40:51,640 --> 01:40:54,159
He doesn't think we will attack the castle.

1156
01:40:54,600 --> 01:40:56,639
The castle will be open to any attack.

1157
01:40:57,200 --> 01:40:59,279
Once the last unity gets out...

1158
01:40:59,480 --> 01:41:01,279
...we'll go in.

1159
01:41:02,800 --> 01:41:06,839
Then we will use the hidden passages.

1160
01:41:07,560 --> 01:41:09,519
Alcicek knows the way.

1161
01:41:09,520 --> 01:41:11,799
She'll show you the way.

1162
01:41:13,760 --> 01:41:15,479
Praise be!

1163
01:41:15,480 --> 01:41:18,759
A daughter in law
has to be like this, right?

1164
01:41:22,960 --> 01:41:24,599
Don't worry.

1165
01:41:24,600 --> 01:41:26,759
We won't reveal your secret.

1166
01:41:27,440 --> 01:41:29,479
We'll go and get out secretly.

1167
01:41:29,480 --> 01:41:31,559
Even the alps of Kargun Tribe...

1168
01:41:31,560 --> 01:41:33,559
...won't see us.

1169
01:41:33,760 --> 01:41:37,519
So that you can keep your
secret with Osman Bey.

1170
01:41:37,520 --> 01:41:39,159
Be careful.

1171
01:41:39,160 --> 01:41:42,959
You'll attack once
we go in and give the sign.

1172
01:41:44,160 --> 01:41:45,639
Come on.

1173
01:41:45,640 --> 01:41:47,919
May our fight be blessed!

1174
01:41:48,200 --> 01:41:49,919
Come on sisters!

1175
01:41:50,560 --> 01:41:51,759
Daughter in law.

1176
01:41:51,760 --> 01:41:53,279
You come with us too.

1177
01:41:53,400 --> 01:41:55,719
As you wish, Hatun The Sister.

1178
01:42:01,760 --> 01:42:03,119
Come on then Kutlu.

1179
01:44:05,320 --> 01:44:07,079
Shaman!

1180
01:44:10,440 --> 01:44:12,599
The poison.

1181
01:44:26,800 --> 01:44:28,199
Osman...

1182
01:44:28,200 --> 01:44:30,599
...with every possible ending...

1183
01:44:30,600 --> 01:44:33,039
...I'm the one who wins.

1184
01:44:34,280 --> 01:44:35,839
Pour it.

1185
01:45:36,360 --> 01:45:38,269
I can't see, Commander Nayman!

1186
01:45:39,090 --> 01:45:41,399
I can't see, Commander Nayman!
I can't see, Commander Nayman!

1187
01:45:56,360 --> 01:45:58,759
Osman’s blind eye...

1188
01:45:59,040 --> 01:46:01,359
...will be my strongest weapon.

1189
01:46:04,600 --> 01:46:06,799
Soldiers!

1190
01:46:08,680 --> 01:46:11,239
Osman dies today..

1191
01:46:11,960 --> 01:46:15,119
..and then his whole family will follow.

1192
01:46:18,560 --> 01:46:19,679
Karancul!

1193
01:46:21,720 --> 01:46:24,319
Bayindir should arrive soon.

1194
01:46:24,720 --> 01:46:28,559
Prepare letters to be sent out
to all Mongol cities!

1195
01:46:29,880 --> 01:46:32,239
Once Bayindir brings the seal here...

1196
01:46:32,600 --> 01:46:35,039
...we will send out the letters.

1197
01:46:35,160 --> 01:46:37,559
As you command, Commander Nayman.

1198
01:46:38,160 --> 01:46:41,279
Osman will' not live long enough...

1199
01:46:41,400 --> 01:46:43,879
...to see me rule over these lands!

1200
01:46:44,400 --> 01:46:48,559
I will erase the word
Turk from all over these lands!

1201
01:46:50,840 --> 01:46:54,359
I will rule the world...

1202
01:46:55,360 --> 01:46:57,279
...with my mighty army!

1203
01:47:26,960 --> 01:47:28,279
Follow me!

1204
01:47:28,440 --> 01:47:30,919
We're leaving!

1205
01:47:54,320 --> 01:47:55,919
Get down!

1206
01:48:37,040 --> 01:48:38,399
Let's go!

1207
01:49:45,051 --> 01:49:46,480
My Bey, as you commanded...

1208
01:49:46,480 --> 01:49:50,109
... Boranand the archer Alps have positioned
behind Nayman and his soldiers.

1209
01:49:53,200 --> 01:49:55,869
Karancu is in charge of
the forces at the base.

1210
01:49:56,160 --> 01:49:59,079
He will water these lands
with blood once Osman is dead!

1211
01:50:53,120 --> 01:50:54,639
Are you ready Osman?

1212
01:50:54,720 --> 01:50:56,239
I am ready!

1213
01:50:57,280 --> 01:50:59,749
I have been waiting for
this moment for a long time!

1214
01:50:59,749 --> 01:51:02,089
Did you give orders to your Beys?

1215
01:51:02,560 --> 01:51:05,479
When you die, they will come
and kneel before me.

1216
01:51:05,560 --> 01:51:07,719
If what you say happens...

1217
01:51:08,640 --> 01:51:10,359
...they will do that.

1218
01:51:11,760 --> 01:51:14,079
But when I take your head...

1219
01:51:15,360 --> 01:51:18,359
...Tell me, will your soldiers
leave these lands?

1220
01:51:18,600 --> 01:51:21,239
It's impossible for you to defeat me.

1221
01:51:21,560 --> 01:51:24,399
...but they will leave if you do.

1222
01:51:25,480 --> 01:51:27,679
They will leave.

1223
01:51:28,640 --> 01:51:30,119
They will.

1224
01:51:30,760 --> 01:51:33,079
But those strong warriors of yours...

1225
01:51:34,000 --> 01:51:36,559
...don't have any chance against my alps.

1226
01:51:37,680 --> 01:51:39,759
The warriors behind me...

1227
01:51:41,280 --> 01:51:43,799
...have been on the road for years.

1228
01:51:44,640 --> 01:51:48,359
My warriors were born in the steppe lands,
they were scorched in the deserts.

1229
01:51:48,640 --> 01:51:51,759
...they were washed in lakes
and they died in battles.

1230
01:51:51,880 --> 01:51:53,279
They became strong!

1231
01:51:53,720 --> 01:51:56,119
You are not strong like iron!

1232
01:51:56,280 --> 01:51:58,759
The warriors you call iron..

1233
01:51:59,160 --> 01:52:03,209
...have been defeated by us many times.
Don't worry.

1234
01:52:04,000 --> 01:52:06,679
My alps will always defeat your warriors.

1235
01:52:06,760 --> 01:52:11,999
Then let's fight your alps and my soldiers!

1236
01:52:12,840 --> 01:52:16,599
Let's warm the field a little
before our fight!

1237
01:52:17,600 --> 01:52:19,439
Send 3 alps.

1238
01:52:19,440 --> 01:52:20,479
What is it?

1239
01:52:21,840 --> 01:52:24,279
Are you scared of death?

1240
01:52:25,440 --> 01:52:28,079
Why aren't you fighting yourself?

1241
01:52:29,320 --> 01:52:33,719
I want to watch my warriors
tear your alps apart.

1242
01:52:35,440 --> 01:52:36,879
Okay.

1243
01:52:38,320 --> 01:52:39,559
Let's do it.

1244
01:52:53,600 --> 01:52:56,359
Mother Sultan, forgive me, but...

1245
01:52:56,360 --> 01:53:00,919
...Even while Sultan Alaeddin agreed
to be allies with Osman Bey...

1246
01:53:01,120 --> 01:53:03,999
Why aren't we on the battlefield?

1247
01:53:04,320 --> 01:53:06,639
That's the point, Celali.

1248
01:53:07,560 --> 01:53:12,759
I thought Osman helped us
sincerely and protected me.

1249
01:53:13,240 --> 01:53:17,559
But he was always planning
his secret move.

1250
01:53:18,400 --> 01:53:21,079
They always have a secret goal.

1251
01:53:21,760 --> 01:53:26,319
First, they took Sultan's support,
then the letter to Gazan Khan.

1252
01:53:28,720 --> 01:53:31,159
But I won't be used, Celali..

1253
01:53:32,680 --> 01:53:34,119
...I am the one who uses!

1254
01:53:34,920 --> 01:53:38,759
From now on, even the most precious
person in these lands...

1255
01:53:39,240 --> 01:53:42,599
...will be nothing but a tool for me!

1256
01:53:57,760 --> 01:54:03,799
Sisters, be cautious. We won't move
until Aktemur and alps enter the castle.

1257
01:54:06,320 --> 01:54:07,679
Come on.

1258
01:54:28,400 --> 01:54:29,959
There is a stone here.

1259
01:54:30,800 --> 01:54:31,919
Give it to me.

1260
01:54:37,000 --> 01:54:38,719
What are you doing Alcicek?

1261
01:54:40,520 --> 01:54:44,119
There is a rope under this rock,
it will open the door.

1262
01:55:22,520 --> 01:55:23,639
It's open.

1263
01:55:25,920 --> 01:55:27,079
Come on.

1264
01:55:42,800 --> 01:55:43,719
Let's go.

1265
01:55:54,160 --> 01:55:56,239
My Bey. I know all their tricks.

1266
01:55:56,960 --> 01:55:59,839
Let me beat them.

1267
01:56:01,000 --> 01:56:01,799
My Bey.

1268
01:56:02,960 --> 01:56:04,719
Allow me to fight.

1269
01:56:06,840 --> 01:56:07,679
My Bey.

1270
01:56:08,080 --> 01:56:09,799
Allow me to battle them.

1271
01:56:10,640 --> 01:56:14,959
My Bey. Allow me to crush
them like a lion.

1272
01:56:16,000 --> 01:56:19,199
My Bey. Let me attack
them like a wolf.

1273
01:56:19,200 --> 01:56:23,879
My Bey. Let my mace
feed on infidel blood.

1274
01:56:27,200 --> 01:56:28,479
Konur.

1275
01:56:30,960 --> 01:56:32,399
Turahan.

1276
01:56:32,480 --> 01:56:33,679
Osman Bey.

1277
01:56:34,320 --> 01:56:38,679
You always choose an Alp.
Let me show you how Beys fight.

1278
01:56:38,680 --> 01:56:41,839
Let me bring you
the corpses of these infidels.

1279
01:56:42,760 --> 01:56:43,799
Bayram Bey.

1280
01:56:45,560 --> 01:56:46,639
Come on then.

1281
01:57:05,000 --> 01:57:07,239
Thank you valiants. Go on.

1282
01:57:09,840 --> 01:57:12,519
Kaucube. Kara Noyan.

1283
01:57:13,160 --> 01:57:14,519
Nogay!

1284
01:57:23,320 --> 01:57:24,319
Warriors!

1285
01:57:25,920 --> 01:57:28,319
May your swords break bones.

1286
01:57:28,560 --> 01:57:31,439
You are Erlik Han's wrath!

1287
01:59:02,920 --> 01:59:21,279
Allah is the Greatest!

1288
01:59:22,560 --> 01:59:23,919
Thank you, my valiant.

1289
01:59:24,080 --> 01:59:25,359
Thank you.

1290
01:59:26,800 --> 01:59:27,759
Turahan.

1291
02:00:45,520 --> 02:00:48,879
Allah is the greatest!

1292
